                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "Mental Shortcuts That Shape Your Reality",
                                    content: "Your brain is an efficiency machine. Rather than carefully analyzing every decision, it uses shortcuts - heuristics - to make quick judgments. These shortcuts are often useful, but they can lead to systematic errors called cognitive biases. Understanding these biases is like gaining a superpower: you can see the invisible forces that shape human behavior.",
