                                        type: "diagram",
                                        svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" class="lesson-visual"><rect x="0" y="0" width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="80" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f59e0b" font-weight="bold" font-size="42">BASE RATE NEGLECT</text><text x="550" y="120" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="26">We ignore statistics when stereotypes feel compelling</text><rect x="100" y="170" width="900" height="130" rx="20" fill="rgba(139,92,246,0.15)" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="215" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b5cf6" font-weight="bold" font-size="26">THE SCENARIO: 1,000 PEOPLE</text><text x="350" y="265" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6366f1" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">995 Librarians</text><text x="750" y="265" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">5 Farmers</text><rect x="100" y="330" width="900" height="100" rx="15" fill="rgba(236,72,153,0.1)" stroke="#ec4899" stroke-width="2"/><text x="550" y="370" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ec4899" font-weight="bold" font-size="24">STEVE: meek, tidy, needs order, passion for detail</text><text x="550" y="410" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="22">Is Steve more likely a librarian or farmer?</text><rect x="100" y="460" width="430" height="220" rx="20" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.15)" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="3"/><text x="315" y="510" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-weight="bold" font-size="26">INTUITIVE ANSWER</text><text x="315" y="560" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="24">"Steve sounds like a librarian"</text><text x="315" y="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="24">Matches the stereotype</text><text x="315" y="660" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="22">Most people say LIBRARIAN</text><rect x="570" y="460" width="430" height="220" rx="20" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.15)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="3"/><text x="785" y="510" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-weight="bold" font-size="26">STATISTICAL REALITY</text><text x="785" y="560" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="24">Even if 10% of librarians</text><text x="785" y="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="24">match = 99 librarians</text><text x="785" y="650" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="22">vs only ~4 matching farmers</text><rect x="150" y="710" width="800" height="150" rx="20" fill="rgba(245,158,11,0.15)" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="760" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f59e0b" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">THE MATH</text><text x="550" y="810" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="24">199 librarians for every 1 farmer in the sample</text><text x="550" y="850" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="22">Base rates MATTER even when descriptions feel compelling</text><rect x="200" y="890" width="700" height="80" rx="15" fill="rgba(255,215,0,0.1)" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2"/><text x="550" y="940" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="24">Always ask: "What's the base rate?" before trusting your gut</text></svg>`,
