                                    content: "System 2 thinking is expensive. It consumes glucose, creates mental fatigue, and requires sustained attention. Your brain, being an efficiency-obsessed machine, avoids using System 2 whenever possible. This laziness explains many of our thinking errors - and why we're often overconfident about judgments we haven't really thought through.",
