                                    content: "The bat-and-ball problem was given to students at Harvard, MIT, and Princeton. Over 50% got it wrong.\n\n**Why?** Intelligence doesn't guarantee engagement of System 2. Smart people are often more confident in their System 1 intuitions.\n\nKahneman: 'The people who answer 10 cents are not stupid - they're just not trying hard enough.'\n\nThe error isn't inability to solve it. The error is not recognizing that careful thought is required.",
