                                    type: "fact",
                                    title: "The Cognitive Ease Principle",
                                    content: "System 2 is LAZY in a very specific way: it defaults to trusting System 1 unless the effort seems necessary. Researchers can make people more careful just by using hard-to-read fonts! The physical difficulty of reading engages System 2. Similarly, unfamiliar accents make people more analytical. **Difficulty of processing = signal to think harder.**",
