                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "Becoming a Better Thinker",
                                    content: "You now understand the machinery of thinking errors. But knowledge isn't enough - even Kahneman admits he still falls for biases. The goal isn't perfection but progress: recognizing the situations where errors are likely, slowing down, and using tools to protect yourself from your own mind. Here's how to actually think better.",
                                    visual: {
                                        type: "diagram",
                                        svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" class="lesson-visual"><rect x="0" y="0" width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="102" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-weight="bold" font-size="42">MAKING BETTER DECISIONS</text><text x="550" y="190" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="28">Practical strategies to outsmart cognitive biases</text><rect x="62" y="293" width="235" height="660" rx="18" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.15)" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="4"/><text x="180" y="385" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">PRE-MORTEM</text><text x="180" y="476" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">Imagine failure</text><text x="180" y="542" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">BEFORE deciding</text><text x="180" y="652" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">"It's a year later.</text><text x="180" y="707" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">This failed. Why?"</text><text x="180" y="843" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">Reduces</text><text x="180" y="898" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">overconfidence</text><rect x="314" y="293" width="235" height="660" rx="18" fill="rgba(245,158,11,0.15)" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="4"/><text x="432" y="385" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f59e0b" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">BASE RATES</text><text x="432" y="476" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">Check what usually</text><text x="432" y="542" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">happens in similar cases</text><text x="432" y="652" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">"What % of startups</text><text x="432" y="707" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">actually succeed?"</text><text x="432" y="843" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">Counters</text><text x="432" y="898" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">planning fallacy</text><rect x="565" y="293" width="235" height="660" rx="18" fill="rgba(99,102,241,0.15)" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="4"/><text x="683" y="385" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6366f1" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">DEVIL'S ADVOCATE</text><text x="683" y="476" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">Assign someone to</text><text x="683" y="542" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">argue the opposite</text><text x="683" y="652" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">Force consideration</text><text x="683" y="707" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">of alternatives</text><text x="683" y="843" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">Fights</text><text x="683" y="898" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">confirmation bias</text><rect x="817" y="293" width="235" height="660" rx="18" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.15)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="4"/><text x="935" y="385" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">SLOW DOWN</text><text x="935" y="476" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">Engage System 2</text><text x="935" y="542" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="28">deliberately</text><text x="935" y="652" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">Sleep on big decisions</text><text x="935" y="707" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="25">Use checklists</text><text x="935" y="843" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">Bypasses</text><text x="935" y="898" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="25">lazy System 2</text><text x="550" y="1026" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f59e0b" font-size="25">Key: Build systems that engage System 2 when it matters most</text></svg>`
                                    }
