                                    type: "fact",
                                    title: "The Takeaway: Recognizing Your Own Blindness",
                                    content: "The final insight from Kahneman: Understanding these biases doesn't make you immune. Even Kahneman admits he falls for anchoring, availability bias, and overconfidence.\n\n**The value isn't immunity - it's recognition**: When you know anchoring exists, you can pause and ask 'Is this anchor biasing me?' When you know availability affects you, you can seek base rates. When you know about overconfidence, you can do pre-mortems.\n\n**Progress, not perfection**: You can't turn off System 1. But you can recognize when to engage System 2. Building this habit - noticing triggers, slowing down, using tools - is how humans make better decisions.",
