                                    content: "Deep in your brain sits two almond-shaped clusters called the amygdala. This ancient structure evolved to keep our ancestors alive by detecting threats instantly.\n\n**The amygdala's job:**\n• Scans incoming information for danger\n• Triggers fight, flight, or freeze responses\n• Stores emotional memories\n• Reacts BEFORE your thinking brain processes what's happening\n\n**The problem:** Your amygdala can't distinguish between a lion attack and a critical email from your boss. It triggers the same alarm response for both."
