                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "What If Perfection Is the Wrong Goal?",
                                    content: "We live in a culture obsessed with flawless skin, optimized routines, and Instagram-perfect lives. But what if this pursuit of perfection is actually making you miserable? Enter **wabi-sabi** — the Japanese aesthetic philosophy that finds beauty in imperfection, impermanence, and incompleteness. A cracked teacup. A weathered wooden beam. The asymmetry of a handmade bowl. Wabi-sabi doesn't tolerate flaws — it celebrates them as evidence of life lived authentically.",
