                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Wabi-Sabi in Everyday Life",
                                    content: "**Sen no Rikyu**, the legendary tea master, chose rough, imperfect tea bowls over polished porcelain. He built his tea rooms small and humble, with natural materials that would age and weather.\n\n**Your worn leather bag** that has shaped itself to your hand over years — that's wabi-sabi.\n\n**The laugh lines on your face** — not flaws to fix, but evidence of joy experienced.\n\n**A meal that didn't turn out perfectly** — but was made with love and eaten with gratitude.\n\n**A friendship that survived conflict** — stronger for having been tested. The gold is in the repair.",
