                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "What If the Best Medicine Grows on Trees?",
                                    content: "In 1982, the Japanese Ministry of Agriculture coined a term: **shinrin-yoku** — 'forest bathing.' It doesn't mean hiking. It doesn't mean exercise. It means slowly, deliberately immersing yourself in the atmosphere of a forest using all your senses. No destination. No fitness goal. Just presence among trees. What sounded like folk wisdom turned out to be hard science. Researchers like **Dr. Qing Li** have spent decades proving that trees aren't just beautiful — they're medicine.",
