                                    content: "You don't live near a forest? That's okay. Dr. Li's research shows benefits from **any meaningful contact with nature**:\n\n**A park with mature trees** — even in a city, phytoncides are present around trees.\n\n**Indoor plants** — studies show rooms with plants reduce stress markers.\n\n**Nature sounds** — recordings of birdsong and flowing water activate the parasympathetic nervous system.\n\n**The key principle**: Shinrin-yoku is about **quality of attention**, not quantity of wilderness. Five minutes of truly present time with a single tree beats an hour of distracted hiking.\n\nThe invitation isn't to move to the forest. It's to **notice the nature that already surrounds you**.",
