                                    title: "Build Your Own Rituals of Presence",
                                    content: "**Your challenge**: Create micro-rituals and practice ma.\n\n1. **Before your first meal today, pause and say** (silently or aloud): 'I receive this.' That's your itadakimasu.\n\n2. **Create a threshold ritual** — When you walk through your front door, take one breath before doing anything else. Mark the transition.\n\n3. **Practice ma in conversation** — In your next meaningful talk, pause for two full seconds before responding. Notice how it changes the quality.\n\n4. **Remove one thing from a space** — A cluttered desk, a crowded shelf. Let one area breathe. That empty space is ma.\n\n**Remember**: Ritual isn't superstition. It's a technology for waking up to your own life.",
