                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Omotenashi as a Way of Living",
                                    content: "Here's the transformative insight: **you don't need to be a hotel host to practice omotenashi**.\n\nEvery interaction is an opportunity to anticipate, to care, to give without keeping score.\n\n**With your partner**: Notice what they need before they ask. A glass of water. A moment of silence. A word of encouragement.\n\n**With a colleague**: Anticipate what would make their day easier. Share information they'll need. Remove a small obstacle.\n\n**With a stranger**: Hold the door not because they're close, but because it's a gift. Make eye contact. Smile first.\n\n**The paradox of omotenashi**: The less you expect in return, the more connected you feel. Selfless giving isn't self-sacrifice — it's **self-expansion**.",
