                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Kaizen in Personal Life",
                                    content: "**Want to read more?** Don't commit to a book a week. Read one page before bed tonight. Tomorrow, maybe two.\n\n**Want to exercise?** Don't buy a gym membership. Do one pushup after brushing your teeth. Add one per week.\n\n**Want to meditate?** Don't aim for 20 minutes. Close your eyes for 60 seconds after your morning coffee.\n\n**Want better relationships?** Don't plan a grand gesture. Send one thoughtful text today.\n\n**The pattern**: Make the first step so small it feels almost ridiculous. That's not weakness — that's strategy. The person who reads one page a night has read 365 pages by year's end. The person who planned to read a book a week often reads zero.",
