                                    title: "What Invisible Threads Hold Your Life Together?",
                                    content: "The Japanese word **musubi** means 'to tie, to bind, to connect.' But it carries a sacred weight far beyond its literal meaning. Musubi is the invisible force that connects you to other people, to nature, to your ancestors, and to the future. It's the spiritual understanding that **no one exists alone** — that your happiness is woven into the happiness of others. In a culture that values interdependence over independence, musubi isn't just a concept. It's the fabric of society.",
