                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Community as Spiritual Practice",
                                    content: "In the musubi worldview, **caring for your community IS your spiritual practice**. There's no separation between 'working on yourself' and 'showing up for others.'\n\nThis challenges the modern Western tendency toward **spiritual individualism** — the idea that growth is a solo journey of retreats, journals, and self-optimization.\n\nMusubi says: **your growth happens in relationship**. You become more yourself through acts of connection, not acts of isolation.\n\nThe person who brings soup to a sick neighbor is practicing musubi.\nThe parent who shows up to every school event is practicing musubi.\nThe friend who remembers what you said three weeks ago is practicing musubi.\n\n**Connection is not a distraction from your path. It IS the path.**",
