                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Your Timeline Is Valid",
                                    content: "Some of the most remarkable people in history bloomed 'late' by conventional standards:\n\n**Vera Wang** designed her first dress at 40. **Julia Child** published her first cookbook at 49. **Colonel Sanders** founded KFC at 62. **Grandma Moses** began painting at 78.\n\nWere they behind? Or were they simply blooming on their own timeline?\n\nOubaitori teaches that **your path doesn't need to match anyone else's calendar**. The person who succeeds at 25 and the person who succeeds at 55 are both right on time — for their own life.\n\n**The only question that matters**: Are you tending your own soil? Are you growing in the direction that's true for you?\n\nCompare yourself to who you were yesterday — not to who someone else is today.",
