                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Oubaitori in Modern Life",
                                    content: "**Career**: Your colleague got the role you wanted. Oubaitori doesn't say 'don't care.' It says: their bloom doesn't diminish yours. Your season is different.\n\n**Relationships**: Friends are getting married and having kids. You're still figuring things out. Oubaitori says: the peach doesn't rush because the plum already bloomed.\n\n**Social media**: Someone's vacation, body, or achievement triggers envy. Oubaitori says: you're seeing one flower's highlight. You don't see their root struggles.\n\n**Learning**: A classmate grasps things faster than you. Oubaitori says: understanding that arrives slowly often roots more deeply.\n\n**The practice**: Every time you catch yourself comparing, whisper: 'Different flower, different season.'",
