                                    title: "The Invitation",
                                    content: "Hiroko Yoda's book doesn't ask you to become Japanese. It asks you to become **more awake**.\n\nMore awake to the beauty in a cracked bowl.\nMore awake to the medicine in a tree.\nMore awake to the preciousness of this passing moment.\nMore awake to the people around you who need to be seen.\nMore awake to your own growth, on your own timeline.\n\n**Eight million ways to happiness** isn't a number. It's a promise: that meaning isn't scarce. It's everywhere. In the steam from your tea. In the silence between words. In the crack that lets the gold in.\n\nYou just have to pay attention.",
