      type: "example",
      title: "Fatima: Love and the Soul of the World",
      content: "At the Al-Fayoum oasis, Santiago meets Fatima — and falls immediately, completely in love.\n\nHe wants to stay. He tells her: *\"I love you. I want to marry you. I'll stay here at the oasis.\"*\n\nFatima's response is one of the most important passages in the novel.\n\nShe says: *\"If you stay here, you'll want to go. And if you go, I'll wait for you — because I am a woman of the desert, and I know that men must follow their Personal Legends.\"*\n\nShe will not ask him to stay. She trusts the Soul of the World.\n\nThe Alchemist later tells Santiago: **\"If what you found is made of pure matter, it will never spoil. And you can always come back.\"** And more pointedly: *\"No heart has ever suffered when it goes in search of its dreams — because every second of the search is a second's encounter with God and with Eternity.\"*\n\nFatima embodies the Soul of the World's wisdom: **Real love does not trap. It frees.** The universe does not conspire against love — it works love into the path.",
