        content: "Melchizedek is one of literature's great mysterious figures. He appears once, gifts Santiago the stones and the truth, and vanishes.\n\nHe tells Santiago he is the **King of Salem** — a title from the Hebrew Bible, associated with the mysterious priest-king who met Abraham.\n\nCoelho uses Melchizedek to embody a spiritual principle: **when you commit to your Personal Legend, the right teacher appears.**\n\nThis is not coincidence. It is the universe conspiring. Melchizedek has appeared to many legends-seekers throughout history. He will appear again after Santiago is long gone.\n\nHis role is not to accompany the journey — it is to **unlock the door** so the journey can begin.\n\nThis is why he takes 1/10 of Santiago's sheep as payment: he is teaching Santiago, from the very first moment, that the legend costs something real.",
