        content: "Coelho doesn't want passive readers — he wants people who live the book.\n\n**This week's practice:**\n\nFor seven days, treat every unexpected event as potentially meaningful. Not superstitiously — but curiously.\n\nWhen something 'random' happens, ask:\n• What was I thinking about just before this happened?\n• Does this feel relevant to any open question in my life?\n• What would I do if this were a message from the universe?\n\n**Advanced practice:** Santiago used the stones to ask yes/no questions when his heart was unclear. You can do the same — flip a coin. But here's the trick: notice how you feel the *instant* the coin lands. Relief or disappointment? That instant reaction is your real answer. The coin just made you admit it.\n\nThe omens were always there. You're just now learning to see them.",
