      type: "intro",
      title: "Fear Is Not a Stop Sign — It's a Compass",
      content: "You've been taught to treat fear as a warning: *danger ahead, turn back.* But Coelho says something radically different.\n\nIn *The Alchemist*, fear is the **clearest signal** that you are moving toward something that matters. The bigger the fear, the closer you are to your Personal Legend.\n\n\"Tell your heart that the fear of suffering is worse than the suffering itself.\"\n\nIn Lesson 7, we break apart how fear works, distinguish the **two types of fear** that paralyze people, explore Santiago's literal conversation with his heart — and build a practice for reading fear as direction rather than prohibition.\n\nBy the end, you'll understand why courage isn't the absence of fear. It's *listening to what the fear is pointing at.*",
