      content: "Quantum physics stumbled onto the Hermetic principle from the other direction. In the double-slit experiment, particles behave differently depending on whether they are being observed. The act of measuring changes what is measured. Your internal attention — what you focus on, what you believe, what you expect — literally changes what you encounter in the external world. This isn't poetry. It's measurable. The inner and outer are not separate systems. They're one system observed from two angles.",
