                                    content: "Most people don't listen to understand—they listen to reply. While others talk, they're preparing their response, filtering through their own experience.\n\n**Seek First to Understand, Then to Be Understood** is about empathic listening: entering another person's frame of reference, seeing the world through their eyes.\n\nThis is the single most important skill in interpersonal relations."
