                                    type: "takeaway",
                                    title: "Key Insight",
                                    content: "Perfectionism isn't about healthy striving—it's armor we use to protect ourselves from shame. But it backfires: the more perfect we try to be, the more shame we feel. The antidote is self-compassion: treating ourselves with the same kindness we'd offer a friend. This isn't weakness or letting yourself off the hook—it's the foundation for real growth."
