                                    title: "Letting Go of Scarcity",
                                    content: "We live in a culture of 'never enough.' Never thin enough, rich enough, successful enough, safe enough. This scarcity mindset makes us afraid of joy—when something good happens, we immediately start bracing for disaster. Brown calls this 'foreboding joy,' and it's one of the most surprising findings of her research."
