                                    content: "Scarcity culture makes us afraid of joy—when something good happens, we immediately brace for disaster. This 'foreboding joy' is how we try to protect ourselves, but it only robs us of the joy that's available right now. The antidote is gratitude: not as a feeling, but as a practice. Those who actively practice gratitude don't fear joy—they lean into it."
