                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Your Circadian Rhythm",
                                    content: "Your circadian rhythm is an internal 24-hour clock controlled by the suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN) in your brain.\n\n**Key facts:**\n• Actually runs slightly longer than 24 hours (~24.2)\n• Reset daily by light exposure (especially morning sunlight)\n• Controls body temperature, hormone release, metabolism\n• Different people have different chronotypes (larks vs. owls)\n\n**Peak alertness:** Usually 10am-12pm and 6pm-8pm\n**Low points:** 2am-4am (danger zone for accidents) and 2pm-4pm (afternoon dip)\n\nThis rhythm persists even without external time cues!",
