                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Key Brain Changes in Trauma",
                                    content: "**Research findings:**\n\n**1. Amygdala (Smoke Alarm)**\n• Becomes hyperactive\n• Triggers false alarms constantly\n• Can't distinguish past from present danger\n\n**2. Medial Prefrontal Cortex (Watchtower)**\n• Becomes underactive\n• Can't regulate the amygdala\n• Rational thought impaired during triggers\n\n**3. Hippocampus (Time-Keeper)**\n• Often shrinks in volume\n• Can't properly timestamp memories\n• Past feels like present\n\n**Good news:** These changes are reversible with proper treatment!"
