                                    title: "Hara Hachi Bu: The 80% Rule",
                                    content: "**Hara hachi bu** = 'Eat until you are 80% full'\n\nThis Confucian teaching, practiced in Okinawa, means:\n• Stop eating before you feel stuffed\n• Leave the table slightly hungry\n• Allow 20 minutes for fullness signals to arrive\n\n**Why it works:**\n• Prevents overeating\n• Reduces caloric intake by ~20%\n• Mimics caloric restriction (proven to extend life)\n• Improves digestion\n\n**How to practice:** Use smaller plates, eat slowly, pause between bites, tune into body signals."
