                                    content: "The business version of Thiel's contrarian question:\n\n**\"What valuable company is nobody building?\"**\n\nThe answer: A company that creates **monopoly**—not through government protection, but through being so good at something unique that no one else can compete.\n\n*\"All happy companies are different: each one earns a monopoly by solving a unique problem. All failed companies are the same: they failed to escape competition.\"*"
