                                    content: "Everyone talks about **first mover advantage**. But Thiel argues the opposite:\n\n**Last mover advantage** is what really matters.\n\nA company's value is the sum of all future profits. Most value comes **years in the future**. The goal isn't to be first—it's to be the **last** significant player in a market."
