                                    type: "application",
                                    title: "Applying the Fundamentals",
                                    content: "**Daily practice:**\n\n**1. Catch yourself before criticizing**\n- Ask: \"Would I want to hear this?\"\n- Reframe as understanding\n\n**2. Find something genuine to appreciate**\n- Be specific, not general\n- Mean it—people detect fakeness\n\n**3. Frame requests around their interests**\n- What do they care about?\n- How does this help them?\n\n*\"If there is any one secret of success, it lies in the ability to get the other person's point of view.\"* — Henry Ford"
