                                    title: "Principle 1: Become Genuinely Interested in Other People",
                                    content: "**The fundamental insight:**\n\nPeople are interested in themselves—morning, noon, and night.\n\n**What this means:**\n- Ask about their lives, interests, and problems\n- Remember what they tell you\n- Follow up on previous conversations\n\n**The paradox:**\nBy being interested in others, you become interesting to them.\n\n**Example:** Theodore Roosevelt impressed everyone he met by remembering details about their lives and asking follow-up questions."
