                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Myth of Rational Negotiation",
                                    content: "Traditional negotiation theory (like *Getting to Yes*) assumes:\n\n- Both parties are rational actors\n- Finding mutual benefit is the goal\n- Splitting the difference leads to fair outcomes\n\n**Reality check**: Humans are emotional, irrational, and unpredictable. We make decisions based on:\n- Fear of loss\n- Need for autonomy\n- Desire for control\n\nSuccessful negotiation acknowledges this emotional reality."
