                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "The 'No-Oriented' Question",
                                    content: "A salesperson kept calling a prospect who wouldn't respond. Traditional approach: *\"Just checking in—do you have time to discuss?\"* (No response.)\n\n**No-oriented approach**: *\"Have you given up on this project?\"*\n\nThe prospect immediately responded: *\"No! We're just swamped. Let's talk next week.\"*\n\nBy framing it as something they would say \"no\" to (giving up), the salesperson triggered their need to correct that assumption. The conversation reopened."
