                                    content: "An ancient Greek parable: *\"The fox knows many things, but the hedgehog knows one big thing.\"*\n\n**Foxes** pursue many strategies simultaneously, seeing the world in all its complexity.\n\n**Hedgehogs** simplify complexity into a single organizing idea—a basic principle that unifies everything.\n\nGood-to-great companies were all hedgehogs. They found their \"one big thing\" and stuck to it with relentless consistency."
