                                    type: "example",
                                    title: "Napoleon's Trap",
                                    content: "Napoleon, despite his reputation for aggression, was a master of making enemies come to him.\n\n**The strategy:**\n• He would position his troops and wait\n• He would feign weakness or offer bait\n• When enemies attacked, they were on his terrain\n• They were exhausted; he was prepared\n\n**The Austerlitz example:**\nNapoleon deliberately weakened his right flank, luring the Allies to attack there. When they committed, he struck their weakened center.\n\nThey came to him—and were destroyed."
