                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "From Earth to the Stars",
                                    content: "On October 4, 1957, a beach-ball-sized satellite named Sputnik beeped its way around Earth, and the Space Age began. In the 67 years since, we've walked on the Moon, landed rovers on Mars, sent probes to every planet, and voyaged to the edge of interstellar space.\n\nSpace exploration represents humanity at its best—curiosity, ingenuity, courage, and cooperation. It's driven by the same impulse that sent our ancestors across oceans and continents: the need to know what lies beyond the horizon.\n\nWe've learned that Earth is a fragile oasis in a vast, mostly hostile cosmos. We've discovered that the raw materials for life are scattered throughout the universe. And we've begun to imagine humanity as a multi-planetary species.\n\nLet's trace the remarkable journey from Sputnik to the stars."
