                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "The Space Race",
                                    content: "The Cold War rivalry between the US and USSR drove rapid advances in space technology:\n\n**Soviet Firsts:**\n• **1957**: Sputnik 1—first artificial satellite\n• **1957**: Laika (dog)—first animal in orbit\n• **1961**: Yuri Gagarin—first human in space\n• **1963**: Valentina Tereshkova—first woman in space\n• **1965**: Alexei Leonov—first spacewalk\n\n**American Achievements:**\n• **1958**: Explorer 1—discovered Van Allen radiation belts\n• **1962**: John Glenn—first American to orbit Earth\n• **1968**: Apollo 8—first humans to orbit the Moon\n• **1969**: Apollo 11—first humans on the Moon (Neil Armstrong, Buzz Aldrin)\n• **1972**: Apollo 17—last Moon landing (so far)\n\n**The Apollo Program:**\n• 12 astronauts walked on the Moon\n• Returned 382 kg of lunar samples\n• Left retroreflectors still used for laser ranging\n• Cost ~$280 billion (2023 dollars)\n• Demonstrated what focused national effort can achieve"
