                                    content: "Robotic spacecraft have visited every planet and many moons, asteroids, and comets:\n\n**Inner Solar System:**\n• **Mercury**: MESSENGER (orbiter), BepiColombo (en route)\n• **Venus**: Venera (Soviet landers), Magellan (radar mapping)\n• **Mars**: 50+ missions, including Curiosity, Perseverance, Ingenuity helicopter\n\n**Outer Solar System:**\n• **Jupiter**: Pioneer 10/11, Voyagers, Galileo, Juno\n• **Saturn**: Pioneer 11, Voyagers, Cassini-Huygens (Titan landing!)\n• **Uranus & Neptune**: Voyager 2 only flyby\n• **Pluto**: New Horizons flyby (2015)\n\n**Small Bodies:**\n• **Comets**: Rosetta landed on 67P, Stardust returned samples\n• **Asteroids**: Hayabusa missions returned samples, OSIRIS-REx\n• **Asteroid deflection**: DART mission successfully changed Dimorphos's orbit\n\n**Interstellar Space:**\n• Voyager 1 crossed the heliopause in 2012—first human-made object in interstellar space\n• Still transmitting data from 24 billion km away"
