                                    content: "Here's the practical framework:\n\n**Step 1: Identify your assumptions**\nWhat do you believe because 'that's how it's done' or 'everyone knows that'? Write them down.\n\n**Step 2: Break the problem into fundamentals**\nWhat are the basic elements? What's actually, physically, provably true? Ignore convention.\n\n**Step 3: Ask 'Why?' until you hit bedrock**\nWhy does it cost so much? â†’ Because of X. Why X? â†’ Because of Y. Keep going until you reach physics, math, or laws of nature.\n\n**Step 4: Build up from the foundation**\nNow that you understand the fundamentals, what NEW solution can you create? You're not constrained by 'how it's always been done.'\n\n**Warning signs you're NOT thinking first principles:**\n• 'That's just how it works'\n• 'Everyone does it this way'\n• 'It's too complex to change'\n• 'The experts say...'\n\n**Feynman's test:** 'Can I recreate this from scratch, or am I just copying?'",
