                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "Your Most Dangerous Enemy",
                                    content: "In his famous 1974 Caltech commencement speech, Feynman said something that should be tattooed on every scientist's forehead—and honestly, on everyone's:\n\n**'The first principle is that you must not fool yourself—and you are the easiest person to fool.'**\n\nThis isn't about lying to others. It's about the subtle ways we deceive ourselves: seeing what we want to see, ignoring inconvenient evidence, and convincing ourselves we understand things we don't.\n\nFeynman called it 'Cargo Cult Science'—doing all the motions of good thinking without actually doing good thinking. This lesson is about recognizing self-deception and developing the intellectual honesty that made Feynman one of science's great truth-seekers.",
