                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "What Would Feynman Explore Today?",
                                    content: "If Feynman were alive today, what would fascinate him? Let's imagine—and maybe inspire your own explorations:\n\n**Technology:**\n• How does machine learning REALLY work? (Not the buzzwords—the actual math)\n• Why do social networks create echo chambers? (First principles analysis)\n• What happens inside a smartphone in one second?\n\n**Science:**\n• What IS dark matter? (We know it exists but not what it is)\n• How do memories form at the molecular level?\n• What makes consciousness possible?\n\n**Everyday Life:**\n• Why do some habits stick and others don't?\n• How does a coffee machine really work?\n• What's actually happening when you fall asleep?\n\n**The pattern:** ANY topic becomes fascinating when approached with genuine curiosity and first principles thinking.\n\n**Your turn:** What mysteries are YOU surrounded by that you've stopped noticing?",
