                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Phases of the Action Potential",
                                    content: "**1. RESTING STATE (-70 mV)**\n• Neuron at resting potential\n• Naâº channels closed, Kâº leak channels open\n• Waiting for stimulus\n\n**2. DEPOLARIZATION (Stimulus â†’ -55 mV â†’ +40 mV)**\n• Stimulus opens voltage-gated Naâº channels\n• Naâº rushes INTO cell (down concentration gradient)\n• Interior becomes more positive\n• **Threshold (-55 mV):** Point of no return!\n• All-or-nothing response begins\n\n**3. REPOLARIZATION (+40 mV â†’ -70 mV)**\n• Naâº channels inactivate (refractory)\n• Voltage-gated Kâº channels open\n• Kâº rushes OUT of cell\n• Interior becomes negative again\n\n**4. HYPERPOLARIZATION (-70 mV â†’ -80 mV â†’ -70 mV)**\n• Kâº channels slow to close\n• Temporarily MORE negative than resting\n• Naâº/Kâº pump restores ion gradients"
