                                {
                                    type: "takeaway",
                                    title: "Key Takeaways: Brain Anatomy",
                                    content: "1. **Three major divisions:** Brainstem (vital functions), cerebellum (coordination), cerebrum (higher cognition)\n\n2. **Brainstem controls survival:** Medulla (heart, breathing), pons (sleep), midbrain (eye movement, reward)\n\n3. **Thalamus relays all sensory info (except smell); hypothalamus controls homeostasis**\n\n4. **Four cortical lobes:** Frontal (executive, motor), parietal (sensation, spatial), temporal (auditory, memory), occipital (vision)\n\n5. **The frontal lobe is uniquely human** controlling planning, personality, and impulse control—and matures last\n\n6. **The brain works as an integrated whole** despite regional specialization"
                                }
