                                    type: "intro",
                                    title: "How You Become You",
                                    content: "In 1953, a man named Henry Molaison (H.M.) had his hippocampi surgically removed to treat severe epilepsy. He was cured—but could never form another new memory. He lived in an eternal present, forgetting conversations within minutes. H.M.'s tragedy revolutionized our understanding of memory, revealing that the brain has multiple memory systems, each stored in different locations. Your memories are quite literally what make you who you are."
