                                    content: "The heart generates its own electrical impulses through specialized cells:\n\n**1. SA Node (Sinoatrial Node)**\n• Location: Right atrium near SVC opening\n• The heart's natural **pacemaker**\n• Fires 60-100 times/minute\n• Sets the heart rate\n\n**2. AV Node (Atrioventricular Node)**\n• Location: Interatrial septum near tricuspid valve\n• **Delays impulse 0.1 seconds** (allows atrial emptying)\n• Backup pacemaker: 40-60 bpm\n\n**3. Bundle of His**\n• Travels through interventricular septum\n• Only electrical connection between atria and ventricles\n\n**4. Right and Left Bundle Branches**\n• Split to supply each ventricle\n• Left bundle has anterior and posterior fascicles\n\n**5. Purkinje Fibers**\n• Spread throughout ventricular walls\n• Conduct impulse rapidly (4 m/s)\n• Backup: 20-40 bpm"
