                                    explanation: "When tissues experience hypoxia (low oxygen), the kidneys release erythropoietin (EPO) to stimulate red bone marrow to produce more RBCs. This is why athletes sometimes illegally use synthetic EPO (blood doping) to increase oxygen-carrying capacity. Chronic kidney disease causes anemia because damaged kidneys produce less EPO."
