                                    content: "WBCs are the immune system's soldiers, divided into two categories:\n\n**Granulocytes** (granules visible, lobed nuclei):\n\n• **Neutrophils (60-70%)** - First responders, phagocytize bacteria\n• **Eosinophils (2-4%)** - Attack parasites, allergic responses\n• **Basophils (0.5-1%)** - Release histamine, allergic reactions\n\n**Agranulocytes** (no visible granules):\n\n• **Lymphocytes (20-25%)**\n  - T cells: Cell-mediated immunity\n  - B cells: Antibody production\n  - NK cells: Kill tumor/virus-infected cells\n\n• **Monocytes (3-8%)**\n  - Become macrophages in tissues\n  - Phagocytize pathogens and debris\n\n**Mnemonic: 'Never Let Monkeys Eat Bananas'**\nNeutrophils > Lymphocytes > Monocytes > Eosinophils > Basophils (frequency order)"
