                                    content: "During exercise, blood flow is dramatically redistributed:\n\n**Increased Flow To:**\n• **Skeletal muscles**: 15% â†’ 85% of cardiac output\n  - Blood flow increases 20-25x\n  - Local vasodilation (metabolites, nitric oxide)\n• **Heart**: Coronary flow increases 4-5x\n• **Skin**: For heat dissipation (later in exercise)\n\n**Decreased Flow To:**\n• **GI tract**: Reduced to 3-5% (from 20-25%)\n• **Kidneys**: Reduced to 2-4% (from 20%)\n• Sympathetic vasoconstriction redirects blood\n\n**The Brain**: Maintains constant flow (~750 mL/min)\n• Autoregulation protects cerebral perfusion\n• Never compromised during exercise\n\n**Key Mechanism:**\nLocal metabolic factors (COâ‚‚, Hâº, adenosine) in working muscles override sympathetic vasoconstriction â†’ **functional sympatholysis**"
