                                    content: "Sports injuries are classified by mechanism and tissue affected:\n\n**By Mechanism:**\n• **Acute/Traumatic** - Single event (fall, collision, twist)\n• **Chronic/Overuse** - Repetitive microtrauma over time\n\n**By Tissue Type:**\n• **Bone** - Fractures, stress fractures\n• **Muscle** - Strains (tears), contusions\n• **Tendon** - Tendinitis, tendinosis, ruptures\n• **Ligament** - Sprains (grades I-III)\n• **Cartilage** - Tears, degeneration\n• **Nerve** - Compression, stretch injuries\n\n**Severity Grading:**\n• **Grade I (Mild)** - Microscopic damage, minimal function loss\n• **Grade II (Moderate)** - Partial tear, moderate function loss\n• **Grade III (Severe)** - Complete tear, significant function loss\n\n**Factors Affecting Injury Risk:**\n• Intrinsic: Age, sex, anatomy, fitness, previous injury\n• Extrinsic: Equipment, surface, training load, technique"
