                                    title: "Common Lower Extremity Injuries",
                                    content: "**Ankle Sprains**\n• Most common athletic injury\n• Usually **inversion** injury (rolling inward)\n• **ATFL** (anterior talofibular ligament) most commonly injured\n• RICE + early mobilization + proprioceptive training\n\n**ACL Tears**\n• Anterior Cruciate Ligament\n• Common in cutting/pivoting sports\n• Often non-contact mechanism\n• Females 2-8× higher risk than males\n• Usually requires surgical reconstruction for athletes\n\n**Meniscus Tears**\n• Cartilage 'shock absorbers' in knee\n• Twisting injury while weight-bearing\n• May occur with ACL injury\n• Symptoms: Locking, catching, swelling\n\n**Hamstring Strains**\n• Most common muscle strain in sports\n• High-speed running most common mechanism\n• Biceps femoris most frequently injured\n• High recurrence rate if not properly rehabilitated\n\n**Achilles Tendinopathy/Rupture**\n• Overuse (tendinopathy) or acute rupture\n• 'Weekend warrior' pattern common\n• Rupture: Sudden 'pop,' can't push off"
