                                    content: "Understanding what happens when training stops:\n\n**Detraining Timeline:**\n• **Cardio fitness:** Declines 4-25% in 3-4 weeks\n• **Strength:** Well-maintained for 2-3 weeks; then gradual loss\n• **Power:** Can decline faster than strength\n• **Muscle mass:** Slower to lose than fitness\n\n**Factors Affecting Detraining:**\n• Training history (longer history = slower loss)\n• Type of fitness (endurance loses faster than strength)\n• Age (older adults may detrain faster)\n• Complete rest vs. reduced training\n\n**Maintenance Training:**\n• Can maintain fitness with reduced volume\n• **Frequency and intensity** more important than volume\n• 1-2 sessions/week may maintain strength\n• ~30% of normal volume can maintain cardio fitness\n\n**Practical Applications:**\n• During busy periods, prioritize frequency over volume\n• Maintain intensity to preserve adaptations\n• Some training >>> no training\n• Planned deload weeks aid long-term progress"
