                                    title: "Critical Thinking in Action",
                                    content: "**Scenario**: You see a headline: \"New Study Shows Coffee Prevents Cancer!\"\n\n**Without Critical Thinking:**\n\"Great! I'll drink more coffee. Science says so!\"\n\n**With Critical Thinking:**\n• Who funded the study? (Coffee industry?)\n• How large was the sample? (10 people or 10,000?)\n• Correlation or causation? (Maybe healthy people drink coffee)\n• What do other studies say? (Is this an outlier?)\n• What does \"prevents\" actually mean? (Reduces risk by 2% or 90%?)\n\n**Result**: You form a **nuanced view** instead of swinging from \"coffee is poison\" to \"coffee is medicine\" based on every new headline.",
