                                    title: "Building Your Argument",
                                    content: "To construct a strong argument, follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1: State Your Conclusion Clearly**\nWhat exactly are you trying to prove? Write it down.\n\n**Step 2: Identify Your Premises**\nWhat must be true for your conclusion to follow?\n\n**Step 3: Check Each Premise**\n• Is it actually true? (Evidence check)\n• Can you prove it? (Or are you assuming it?)\n• Will your audience accept it?\n\n**Step 4: Verify the Logic**\nDoes the conclusion NECESSARILY follow? Or just probably?\n\n**Step 5: Steel Man the Opposition**\nWhat's the strongest counter-argument? Address it.\n\n**Step 6: Qualify Appropriately**\n\"Probably,\" \"likely,\" \"evidence suggests\" - match confidence to evidence.",
