                                    title: "The Clustering Illusion",
                                    content: "We see patterns in randomness. The **clustering illusion** makes us perceive streaks or clusters in random data as meaningful. A basketball player hitting several shots in a row feels 'hot'—but statistical analysis shows 'hot hand' streaks are exactly what randomness predicts. **Random data clumps naturally**; our pattern-seeking brains see false meaning."
