                                    type: "concept",
                                    title: "Joint Movements",
                                    content: "**ANGULAR MOVEMENTS:**\n• **Flexion** - decrease angle (bending)\n• **Extension** - increase angle (straightening)\n• **Hyperextension** - beyond anatomical position\n• **Abduction** - away from midline\n• **Adduction** - toward midline\n• **Circumduction** - circular movement\n\n**ROTATION:**\n• **Medial/Internal** - toward midline\n• **Lateral/External** - away from midline\n\n**SPECIAL MOVEMENTS:**\n• **Supination** - palm up (\"hold a bowl of soup\")\n• **Pronation** - palm down (\"prone position\")\n• **Dorsiflexion** - toes up\n• **Plantar flexion** - toes down (like stepping on gas)\n• **Inversion** - sole faces medially\n• **Eversion** - sole faces laterally\n• **Protraction/Retraction** - forward/backward (jaw)\n• **Elevation/Depression** - up/down (shoulders)"
