                                    content: "**THE HEART'S ELECTRICAL SYSTEM:**\n\n**1. SA NODE (Sinoatrial Node)**\n• \"Pacemaker\" of the heart\n• Right atrium\n• Sets heart rate (60-100 bpm normally)\n• Generates action potential spontaneously\n\n**2. AV NODE (Atrioventricular Node)**\n• Between atria and ventricles\n• Delays signal (allows atria to empty)\n• Only electrical connection between atria/ventricles\n\n**3. BUNDLE OF HIS**\n• Conducts through interventricular septum\n\n**4. BUNDLE BRANCHES**\n• Right and Left branches\n• Carry signal down septum\n\n**5. PURKINJE FIBERS**\n• Spread signal through ventricular walls\n• Rapid conduction â†’ coordinated contraction\n\n**ECG/EKG reflects this:**\n• P wave = atrial depolarization\n• QRS complex = ventricular depolarization\n• T wave = ventricular repolarization"
