                                    explanation: "42 CFR Part 2 requires specific written patient consent with 10 mandatory elements for disclosure of substance abuse treatment records. While the 2024 final rule now allows TPO sharing with general consent, the consent requirement itself remains mandatory. A HIPAA authorization alone is insufficient — Part 2 has its own specific consent requirements that must be met. Court orders are required for law enforcement access, not treatment transfers.",
                                    visual: {
                                        type: "diagram",
                                        svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" class="lesson-visual"><rect x="0" y="0" width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-weight="bold" font-size="42">PART 2 CONSENT</text><text x="550" y="100" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="29">10 Required Elements</text><rect x="150" y="140" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="175" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">1. Name of patient</text><rect x="150" y="210" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="245" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">2. Name of program making disclosure</text><rect x="150" y="280" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="315" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">3. Name of recipient</text><rect x="150" y="350" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="385" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">4. Purpose of disclosure</text><rect x="150" y="420" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="455" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">5. How much and what kind of information</text><rect x="150" y="490" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="525" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">6. Patient signature</text><rect x="150" y="560" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="595" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">7. Date signed</text><rect x="150" y="630" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="665" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">8. Statement of right to revoke</text><rect x="150" y="700" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="735" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">9. Expiration date/event/condition</text><rect x="150" y="770" width="800" height="55" rx="12" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)"/><text x="200" y="805" text-anchor="start" fill="#fff" font-size="20">10. Prohibition on redisclosure statement</text></svg>`,
                                        caption: "42 CFR Part 2 requires all 10 consent elements — more than HIPAA's 6"
                                    }
