                                    explanation: "When health records are maintained by an educational institution that receives federal education funding, FERPA — not HIPAA — is the governing law. The campus clinic is part of the university, making these education records under FERPA. If the university had a separately HIPAA-covered health clinic, HIPAA would apply to that clinic's records. 42 CFR Part 2 only applies to federally assisted substance abuse programs, and GINA covers genetic information discrimination, neither of which applies here.",
