                                    type: "quiz",
                                    question: "Which of the following would make a breach of PHI NOT reportable under the Breach Notification Rule?",
                                    options: [
                                        { text: "The breach affected fewer than 500 individuals", correct: false },
                                        { text: "The PHI was encrypted using NIST-approved algorithms at the time of the incident", correct: true },
                                        { text: "The entity immediately terminated the responsible employee", correct: false },
                                        { text: "The entity reported the breach to local law enforcement", correct: false }
                                    ],
                                    explanation: "If PHI is properly encrypted using NIST-approved algorithms, it is considered SECURED PHI. The breach notification rule only applies to UNSECURED PHI. If the data was encrypted and the encryption key was not compromised, it is not a reportable breach regardless of how many individuals were affected. The number of individuals doesn't determine if it's a breach — it only determines the notification timeline. Terminating the employee and reporting to law enforcement are appropriate responses but don't change the breach reporting obligation.",
