                                    explanation: "Title VI requires qualified medical interpreters for LEP patients — trained professionals who understand medical terminology and maintain patient confidentiality. Using minor children is specifically prohibited as it places an inappropriate burden on the child and may result in inaccurate translation. Untrained bilingual staff (like housekeeping) lack medical terminology knowledge. Telling patients to find their own translator fails to provide meaningful access. Video Remote Interpreting (VRI) and telephone language lines are acceptable alternatives to in-person interpreters.",
