      {
        type: "quiz",
        question: "Under EMTALA, what is the first obligation of a hospital when a person presents to the emergency department?",
        options: [
          { text: "Verify the patient's insurance coverage", correct: false },
          { text: "Provide a Medical Screening Examination (MSE)", correct: true },
          { text: "Transfer the patient to a public hospital", correct: false },
          { text: "Obtain a signed financial responsibility agreement", correct: false }
        ],
        explanation: "EMTALA requires that any person who comes to an ED requesting examination or treatment must receive an appropriate Medical Screening Examination (MSE) to determine whether an Emergency Medical Condition (EMC) exists. This must occur regardless of ability to pay — hospitals CANNOT ask about insurance before the MSE. If an EMC is found, the hospital must stabilize before transfer or discharge.",
        visual: { type: "diagram", svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" class="lesson-visual"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" font-size="42" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Quiz: EMTALA</text><text x="550" y="100" font-size="29" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">Emergency Treatment Mandate</text><rect x="60" y="150" width="980" height="200" rx="18" fill="#23234a"/><text x="100" y="195" font-size="26" fill="#10b981" font-weight="bold">EMTALA Sequence</text><text x="100" y="235" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700">1.</text><text x="140" y="235" font-size="22" fill="#fff">Patient arrives at ED requesting care</text><text x="100" y="270" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700">2.</text><text x="140" y="270" font-size="22" fill="#fff">Hospital provides MSE (cannot ask about insurance first!)</text><text x="100" y="305" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700">3.</text><text x="140" y="305" font-size="22" fill="#fff">If EMC found → stabilize before transfer/discharge</text><text x="100" y="340" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700">4.</text><text x="140" y="340" font-size="22" fill="#fff">If cannot stabilize → appropriate transfer with documentation</text></svg>`, caption: "Illustration" }
      },
      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Apply It: 20th Century Laws & Daily HIM Work",
        content: "Every major 20th-century healthcare law directly creates HIM responsibilities: (1) Blue Cross/Blue Shield and commercial insurance require claims processing — HIM codes diagnoses and procedures for billing. (2) Hill-Burton's free care obligation requires tracking charity care patients in the billing system. (3) Medicare/Medicaid require meticulous documentation for reimbursement — every DRG assignment, every CPT code, every modifier must be supported by the medical record. (4) HMO/managed care requires utilization review documentation, prior authorizations, and referral tracking. (5) DRGs made coding accuracy a revenue issue — HIM departments now have coding compliance programs, internal audits, and Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) programs. (6) EMTALA requires documented MSE, stabilization, and transfer documentation. (7) HIPAA's Privacy and Security Rules define how HIM handles every Release of Information (ROI) request, manages access controls, conducts breach investigations, and ensures every electronic transaction uses standardized formats. As an HIM professional, you are the guardian of compliance with ALL of these laws simultaneously.",
        visual: { type: "diagram", svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" class="lesson-visual"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" font-size="42" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Apply It: Daily HIM Work</text><text x="550" y="100" font-size="29" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">Every Law Creates HIM Responsibilities</text><rect x="60" y="135" width="470" height="110" rx="14" fill="#23234a" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="170" font-size="20" fill="#3b82f6" font-weight="bold">Insurance Claims</text><text x="100" y="200" font-size="18" fill="#fff">Code dx/procedures for Blue Cross,</text><text x="100" y="225" font-size="18" fill="#fff">commercial, and government payers</text><rect x="570" y="135" width="470" height="110" rx="14" fill="#23234a" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="610" y="170" font-size="20" fill="#10b981" font-weight="bold">DRG Accuracy</text><text x="610" y="200" font-size="18" fill="#fff">Coding compliance, CDI programs,</text><text x="610" y="225" font-size="18" fill="#fff">internal audits — revenue integrity</text><rect x="60" y="265" width="470" height="110" rx="14" fill="#23234a" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="300" font-size="20" fill="#f59e0b" font-weight="bold">Utilization Review</text><text x="100" y="330" font-size="18" fill="#fff">Prior auth documentation,</text><text x="100" y="355" font-size="18" fill="#fff">referral tracking for managed care</text><rect x="570" y="265" width="470" height="110" rx="14" fill="#23234a" stroke="#ec4899" stroke-width="2"/><text x="610" y="300" font-size="20" fill="#ec4899" font-weight="bold">EMTALA Compliance</text><text x="610" y="330" font-size="18" fill="#fff">MSE documentation, transfer forms,</text><text x="610" y="355" font-size="18" fill="#fff">stabilization records</text><rect x="60" y="395" width="980" height="110" rx="14" fill="#23234a" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="430" font-size="20" fill="#8b5cf6" font-weight="bold">HIPAA Compliance (Every Single Day)</text><text x="100" y="460" font-size="18" fill="#fff">ROI requests, access controls, breach investigations, privacy training,</text><text x="100" y="485" font-size="18" fill="#fff">standardized transactions, audit trails, Notice of Privacy Practices</text><rect x="60" y="530" width="980" height="80" rx="18" fill="#1e1e3a" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="575" font-size="22" fill="#ffd700" font-weight="bold">HIM = Guardian of compliance with ALL these laws simultaneously</text></svg>`, caption: "Illustration" }
      }
