            content: "The U.S. healthcare workforce is one of the largest employment sectors in the nation, with over **22 million workers** according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS). Healthcare employs more people than any other industry in the United States.\n\nThis lesson covers the major categories of healthcare professionals — from physicians and mid-level providers to nurses, allied health professionals, and HIM specialists. Understanding **scope of practice**, **credentialing**, **licensure**, and **workforce trends** is critical for HIM professionals who work alongside all of these roles.\n\nKey concepts include:\n• **Licensure** — State-granted legal authority to practice (mandatory)\n• **Certification** — Voluntary credential from a professional body demonstrating competence\n• **Credentialing** — The process of verifying a provider's qualifications (education, training, licensure, certification)\n• **Privileging** — A healthcare facility granting specific clinical activities a provider may perform\n\nThe distinction between **licensure** (government-mandated) and **certification** (voluntary, professional) is a common exam question.",
