            title: "Healthcare Financing Fundamentals",
            content: "The United States spent approximately **$4.8 trillion** on healthcare in 2023, accounting for **17.3% of GDP** — far more than any other developed nation. The **Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS)** projects national health expenditures (NHE) will reach **$7.2 trillion by 2031**.\n\nUnderstanding how money flows through the healthcare system is fundamental for HIM professionals. Every code you assign, every document you manage, and every data element you validate has a direct financial impact.\n\n**Key Questions This Lesson Answers:**\n• How does revenue flow from patient encounter to payment?\n• What is the difference between fee-for-service and value-based payment?\n• How do claims get processed and paid?\n• What is a chargemaster and why does it matter?\n• How do hospitals track costs and manage their finances?\n• Who actually pays for healthcare in America?\n\nThe **revenue cycle** is the financial backbone of every healthcare organization, and HIM sits at its center — coding drives reimbursement, documentation supports medical necessity, and data integrity ensures compliance.",
