            explanation: "The ACA marketplace uses **metal tiers** to categorize plans by **actuarial value** — the average percentage of total healthcare costs the plan covers. **Gold plans have an 80% actuarial value**, meaning the plan covers about 80% of costs on average, and the enrollee covers 20%. The tiers are: **Bronze (60%)**, **Silver (70%)**, **Gold (80%)**, **Platinum (90%)**. Higher metal tier = higher premium but lower out-of-pocket costs. Bronze has the lowest premium but highest patient cost-sharing. Platinum has the highest premium but lowest patient cost-sharing. A **Catastrophic plan** (<60% AV) is also available for those under 30 or with hardship exemptions.",
