            explanation: "Deemed status means CMS has determined that an accrediting organization's standards meet or exceed the CMS Conditions of Participation. When a facility is accredited by an organization with deemed status (such as The Joint Commission or DNV GL Healthcare), it is 'deemed' to meet CMS requirements and does not need a separate CMS certification survey. This is why most hospitals pursue TJC or DNV accreditation -- it simultaneously satisfies the federal participation requirement. However, CMS retains the right to conduct its own validation surveys.",
