            explanation: "The HRRP, established by ACA Section 3025, penalizes hospitals with excess 30-day readmission rates by reducing ALL Medicare DRG payments by up to 3%. This is not limited to the specific conditions measured — it applies to the hospital's ENTIRE Medicare inpatient payment. The conditions tracked include AMI, heart failure, pneumonia, COPD, THA/TKA, and CABG. The HAC Reduction Program has a 1% maximum penalty. Loss of Medicare certification is an extreme action used for Conditions of Participation violations, not HRRP.",
