            explanation: "The key distinction is INTEROPERABILITY. An EMR (Electronic Medical Record) is the digital version of a paper chart within ONE organization — it does not easily share data outside those walls. An EHR (Electronic Health Record) is designed to share information ACROSS organizations — hospitals, specialists, labs, pharmacies. EHRs meet interoperability standards, support HIE, and are the focus of federal certification programs. Patient-maintained records are PHRs (Personal Health Records), not EHRs.",
