            options: [
                { text: "The specification is optional and can be skipped if the entity chooses", correct: false },
                { text: "The entity must assess it, and either implement it, implement an alternative, or document why neither is reasonable", correct: true },
                { text: "The specification only applies to large healthcare organizations with 500+ employees", correct: false },
                { text: "The specification must be addressed within one year of the compliance deadline", correct: false }
            ],
            explanation: "This is one of the MOST TESTED HIPAA concepts. 'Addressable' does NOT mean optional. The entity must: (1) Assess whether the specification is reasonable and appropriate in their environment, (2) If yes, implement it, (3) If no, document the justification AND implement an equivalent alternative measure if reasonable, OR document why no alternative is feasible. You must make a DOCUMENTED, REASONED DECISION. Simply ignoring an addressable specification is a violation. Examples of addressable specifications include encryption at rest and automatic logoff.",
