            content: "The ACA implemented sweeping reforms to the health insurance market, fundamentally changing how insurers operate:\n\n**Guaranteed Issue**\n• Insurers MUST accept all applicants regardless of health status\n• No preexisting condition exclusions for any individual or group plan\n• Effective for children in 2010, all individuals January 1, 2014\n\n**Community Rating (Modified)**\n• Premiums can only vary based on: (1) Age (max 3:1 ratio), (2) Tobacco use (max 1.5:1), (3) Geography, (4) Family size\n• CANNOT vary by: health status, gender, claims history, occupation, genetic information\n\n**Medical Loss Ratio (MLR) — The 80/20 Rule**\n• Individual and small group plans must spend at least **80%** of premiums on clinical services and quality improvement\n• Large group plans must spend at least **85%**\n• If insurers fail to meet MLR, they must issue **rebates** to enrollees\n• MLR = (Clinical costs + Quality improvement) / Total premium revenue\n\n**Dependent Coverage**\n• Young adults can stay on parents' insurance until age **26** regardless of student status, marital status, financial dependence, or availability of employer coverage\n• One of the most popular ACA provisions\n\n**No Annual or Lifetime Dollar Limits**\n• Insurers cannot impose annual or lifetime dollar limits on essential health benefits\n• Previously, many plans had $1M or $2M lifetime caps",
