            content: "The ACA fundamentally transformed the HIM profession by making **data accuracy** a direct driver of organizational revenue and compliance:\n\n**1. Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI)**\n• Value-based programs require accurate severity/risk documentation\n• CDI specialists bridge clinical and coding accuracy\n• Inaccurate documentation → missed quality measures → reduced payment\n\n**2. Quality Reporting & Measures**\n• Hospital VBP, HRRP, HAC programs all rely on coded data\n• HIM professionals ensure accurate capture of present-on-admission (POA) indicators\n• CMS quality measures derived from claims data depend on correct ICD-10-CM/PCS coding\n\n**3. Risk Adjustment**\n• Marketplace plans and Medicare Advantage use **HCC (Hierarchical Condition Category)** risk adjustment\n• Accurate coding directly affects plan payments — undercoding loses revenue, overcoding triggers audits\n• Risk Adjustment Data Validation (RADV) audits by CMS verify coding accuracy\n\n**4. Electronic Health Records**\n• ACA complemented HITECH Act EHR incentives\n• Meaningful Use / Promoting Interoperability measures tied to reimbursement\n• HIM manages data governance, integrity, and interoperability standards\n\n**5. Population Health Analytics**\n• HIM data feeds population health dashboards, disease registries, care gap identification\n• ACO success depends on accurate attribution and quality measurement — driven by coded data",
