            content: "**HIM Professional Task: Help your CFO understand which value-based models apply to your health system.**\n\nYour organization is a 400-bed hospital with:\n• 200 employed physicians (Medicare Part B billers)\n• An ACO with 15,000 attributed Medicare beneficiaries\n• High HF and pneumonia readmission rates\n\n**Which models affect your revenue?**\n\n**MIPS** — All 200 physicians are scored on Quality (30%), PI (25%), IA (15%), Cost (30%). Maximum ±9% adjustment on Part B payments. Poor scores = organization-wide revenue loss.\n\n**Hospital VBP** — Your hospital's DRG payments are partially withheld and redistributed based on quality performance. Must perform above average to earn net positive.\n\n**HRRP** — With high readmission rates, your hospital faces up to **3% Medicare payment reduction**. Immediate priority: reduce HF and pneumonia readmissions.\n\n**HAC Reduction** — If in bottom 25% by HAC score, another 1% Medicare cut.\n\n**MSSP** — Your ACO's spending vs. benchmark determines shared savings. Quality reporting required. Accurate HCC coding affects both ACO benchmark setting and quality scores.\n\n**HIM Actions:**\n1. Prioritize CDI for HF documentation specificity (I50.22 vs I50.9)\n2. Ensure annual HCC recapture for all chronic conditions\n3. Verify POA indicators to avoid HAC misattribution\n4. Support MIPS quality measure reporting through accurate coding\n5. Train coding staff on risk adjustment implications\n\nThis is how HIM directly impacts the bottom line in value-based care.",
