      content: `## Welcome to Lesson 1

The **healthcare revenue cycle** is the complete financial process that begins the moment a patient schedules an appointment and ends when the provider receives full payment.

Every interaction — from verifying insurance to posting a payment — is a link in this chain. A break anywhere creates delays, denials, and lost revenue.

**In this lesson you will learn:**
- The three phases of the revenue cycle
- How Health Information Management (HIM) fits in
- Key performance indicators (KPIs) that measure success
- How to spot a real-world revenue problem and fix it`,
