      title: "Back-End Phase: Claims, A/R, and Denials",
      content: `## The Back-End Phase

The back-end phase focuses on **converting billed claims into collected cash**.

### Key Functions

**Claims Submission**
Clean claims submitted electronically to payers. Must pass scrubbing edits before transmission.

**Accounts Receivable (A/R) Management**
Tracking outstanding balances and following up on unpaid claims. Goal: minimize Days in A/R.

**Denial Management**
Identifying, appealing, and resolving denied claims. Also analyzing denial trends to prevent future denials.

**Payment Posting**
Recording payer and patient payments accurately to the correct account.

**Patient Collections**
Collecting residual patient balances after insurance adjudication.

### The Denial Cycle
\`\`\`
Claim denied → Identify reason → Gather documentation →
Appeal within timely filing → Resubmit → Collect
\`\`\`

> ⚠️ **Timely Filing Limits**: Most payers allow 90–365 days from service date. Missed deadlines = uncollectable write-offs.`,
