      content: `# Who Pays the Bill?

In healthcare billing, understanding **who pays** is as important as knowing **what was done**. Payers are the entities that reimburse providers for services rendered.

## The Major Categories

- **Government Programs** — Medicare, Medicaid, CHIP, TRICARE
- **Commercial Insurance** — employer-sponsored and individual plans
- **Self-Pay** — patients paying out-of-pocket

## Why This Matters

Each payer has its own:
- **Rules** for covered services
- **Fee schedules** for reimbursement
- **Timely filing** deadlines
- **Coordination of benefits** requirements

Misidentifying the primary payer is one of the top causes of claim denials. By the end of this lesson, you'll know how to determine who pays first — every time.`,
