      content: `# Medicare Overview

Medicare is a **federal health insurance program** primarily for people 65+ and certain younger individuals with disabilities or end-stage renal disease (ESRD).

## The Four Parts

| Part | Name | Covers |
|------|------|--------|
| **A** | Hospital Insurance | Inpatient hospital, skilled nursing, hospice, home health |
| **B** | Medical Insurance | Outpatient, physician visits, preventive services, DME |
| **C** | Medicare Advantage | Parts A+B+often D bundled via private insurer |
| **D** | Prescription Drug | Outpatient prescription medications |

## Key Billing Facts

- **Part A** — No premium for most (paid through payroll taxes); deductible per benefit period
- **Part B** — Monthly premium required; 80/20 coinsurance after deductible
- **Part C** — Patient enrolls in an MA plan instead of Original Medicare; billed to the plan
- **Part D** — Separate drug plan; formulary varies by plan

## Original Medicare vs. Medicare Advantage

- **Original Medicare** = Parts A + B (government pays directly)
- **Medicare Advantage** = Private plan approved by CMS; must cover same services as Original Medicare`,
