      content: `# Commercial Payer Plan Types

Commercial (private) insurance comes in several plan designs. Knowing the plan type determines network rules and billing strategy.

## The Four Main Plan Types

### HMO — Health Maintenance Organization
- **Must use in-network providers** (except emergencies)
- **Requires a Primary Care Physician (PCP)** as gatekeeper
- **Referrals required** for specialist visits
- Lower premiums; no out-of-network coverage

### PPO — Preferred Provider Organization
- **Can see any provider** in or out of network
- **No PCP or referral** required
- Higher premiums; out-of-network covered at lower rate
- Most flexible plan type

### EPO — Exclusive Provider Organization
- **Must stay in-network** (like HMO)
- **No referrals required** (like PPO)
- No out-of-network coverage (except emergencies)
- Middle ground on premiums

### HDHP — High Deductible Health Plan
- **High deductible** before insurance pays (min $1,600 individual / $3,200 family in 2024)
- Often paired with an **HSA (Health Savings Account)**
- Lower premiums; patient pays more upfront
- Can be offered as HMO, PPO, or EPO structure

## Billing Impact

| Plan | Check Network? | Need Referral? | Out-of-Network Covered? |
|------|---------------|---------------|------------------------|
| HMO | Always | Yes | No |
| PPO | Recommended | No | Yes (less) |
| EPO | Always | No | No |
| HDHP | Varies | Varies | Varies |`,
