      title: "Claim Forms: UB-04 & CMS-1500",
      content: `## The Two Pillars of Healthcare Billing

Every healthcare claim travels on one of two standard forms — chosen based on **who treated you** and **where**.

| Form | Used By | EDI Transaction |
|------|---------|-----------------|
| **UB-04** (CMS-1450) | Hospitals, facilities, SNFs | 837I (Institutional) |
| **CMS-1500** | Physicians, outpatient providers | 837P (Professional) |

Getting the wrong form to the wrong payer = **instant rejection**.

In this lesson you will:
- Master the critical form locators (FLs) on the UB-04
- Identify the key boxes on the CMS-1500
- Distinguish 837I vs 837P EDI transactions
- Understand claim scrubbing, rejections, and denials
- Apply a clean-claim checklist before submission`,
