      type: "concept",
      title: "UB-04: Purpose & Structure",
      content: `## What Is the UB-04?

The **UB-04** (Uniform Bill 2004) is the standardized paper claim form used by **institutional providers** — hospitals, skilled nursing facilities, home health agencies, and hospice organizations.

### Why It Exists
Institutional billing is complex: a single inpatient stay may span multiple days, involve dozens of procedures, and require per-diem revenue codes. The UB-04 consolidates all charges onto one form with structured **Form Locators (FLs)** numbered 1–81.

### Key Structural Sections

| Section | FLs | Contains |
|---------|-----|----------|
| Patient/Facility Info | FL1–FL17 | Provider name, patient ID, dates |
| Condition/Occurrence | FL18–FL36 | Codes explaining special circumstances |
| Value/Revenue Codes | FL39–FL49 | Revenue codes, units, charges |
| Diagnosis/Procedure | FL67–FL81 | ICD-10 codes, principal Dx, procedures |

### Revenue Codes
UB-04 uses **4-digit revenue codes** (e.g., 0120 = Medical/Surgical Bed, 0450 = Emergency Room) to categorize each type of charge. These do not appear on the CMS-1500.

> **Key Rule:** Every UB-04 must have a principal diagnosis (FL67) and at least one revenue code line — without these, the claim will fail scrubbing.`,
