      type: "concept",
      title: "UB-04 Key Form Locators",
      content: `## Critical Form Locators You Must Know

The UB-04 has 81 form locators. These five are the most frequently tested and error-prone:

### FL4 — Type of Bill (TOB)
A **3-digit code** that tells the payer: who you are, what kind of care was given, and where in the billing sequence this claim falls.

- **1st digit**: Facility type (1=Hospital, 2=SNF, 3=Home Health…)
- **2nd digit**: Bill classification (1=Inpatient, 3=Outpatient, 4=Other Outpatient…)
- **3rd digit**: Frequency (1=Admit through discharge, 2=Interim-first, 7=Replacement)

> Example: **TOB 111** = Hospital Inpatient, Admit-through-Discharge claim

### FL6 — Statement Covers Period (From / Through)
The **date range** covered by this claim. For inpatient, this is admission date through discharge date. Gaps or overlaps trigger payer edits.

### FL67 — Principal Diagnosis Code
The **ICD-10-CM code** for the condition chiefly responsible for the admission — must be the most specific valid code available.

### FL74 — Principal Procedure Code & Date
The **ICD-10-PCS code** for the principal procedure performed during an inpatient stay, plus the date performed. (Outpatient claims use CPT/HCPCS on the revenue code line instead.)

### FL82–83 — Attending & Other Provider
NPI numbers for the **attending physician** (FL82) and other operating/rendering providers (FL83). Missing or invalid NPIs are a top rejection reason.`,
