      type: "concept",
      title: "CMS-1500: Purpose & Key Fields",
      content: `## The CMS-1500 Professional Claim

The **CMS-1500** (version 02/12) is the universal claim form for **professional/physician services**. It uses numbered **boxes** (1–33) rather than form locators.

### Form Sections at a Glance

| Boxes | Section |
|-------|---------|
| 1–13 | Patient and insured information |
| 14–33 | Physician/supplier information |

### Box 21 — Diagnosis Codes
Up to **12 ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes** labeled A–L. Each service line in Box 24 references these letters to link the diagnosis to the procedure.

### Box 24 — Service Line Detail (A–J columns)
The heart of the claim — up to **6 service lines**, each containing:
- **24A**: Date(s) of service (from / to)
- **24B**: Place of Service (POS) code (11=Office, 21=Inpatient Hospital, 23=ER…)
- **24D**: Procedure code (CPT or HCPCS) + modifiers
- **24E**: Diagnosis pointer (links to Box 21 letter)
- **24F**: Charges
- **24G**: Units (days or units)
- **24J**: Rendering provider NPI

### Box 33 — Billing Provider
The **billing provider's** name, address, and NPI (Box 33a). This is the entity being paid — may differ from the rendering provider in Box 24J.

> **Modifier Rule:** Modifiers in Box 24D can change payment (e.g., -25 = significant separate E/M same day as procedure; -59 = distinct procedural service). Incorrect modifiers → downcoding or denial.`,
