      content: `## Definition & Purpose

The **Chargemaster** (also called the **Charge Description Master** or **CDM**) is a comprehensive, facility-maintained database listing every service, supply, procedure, and accommodation a hospital or healthcare facility can bill.

### Why It Exists
- Provides a **standardized price list** for all billable items
- Ensures **consistent coding** across all claims
- Serves as the bridge between clinical documentation and billing
- Required by CMS for all Medicare/Medicaid participating facilities

### Key Characteristics
| Feature | Detail |
|---|---|
| Scope | All departments — lab, pharmacy, radiology, surgery, ED, etc. |
| Size | Community hospitals: 10,000–20,000 line items; Large academic: 30,000+ |
| Ownership | Revenue Cycle / Finance (with clinical input) |
| Update Frequency | Ongoing; major review annually |

> The CDM is **not** a fee schedule — it lists the facility's **gross charges** before any contractual adjustments or discounts are applied.`,
