      title: "Revenue Code Categories",
      content: `## Revenue Codes: Classifying What Was Provided

Revenue codes are **4-digit codes** (shown as 3-digit + subcategory) standardized by the **National Uniform Billing Committee (NUBC)**. They classify the **type of service or accommodation** on the UB-04 claim form.

### Key Revenue Code Ranges

| Range | Category | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **010x** | Room & Board – General | 0101 = Medical/Surgical Private |
| **013x** | Room & Board – ICU | 0131 = ICU Private |
| **036x** | Pharmacy | 0360 = General Pharmacy |
| **045x** | Emergency Room | 0450 = General ER |
| **030x** | Laboratory | 0300 = General Lab |
| **032x** | Radiology – Diagnostic | 0320 = General Radiology |
| **042x** | Physical Therapy | 0420 = General PT |
| **027x** | Medical/Surgical Supplies | 0270 = Non-sterile supplies |

### Important Rules
- Revenue code **0001** = total charges line (always required on UB-04)
- Some revenue codes **require** a matching CPT/HCPCS code (e.g., surgery, lab)
- Others **do not** require CPT (e.g., room and board accommodations)
- Payers use revenue codes to **route claims** to correct adjudication logic

> Tip: The third digit of the revenue code usually indicates the subcategory. "0" = general/other for most categories.`,
