      type: "concept",
      title: "DRG Grouper Logic: MDC → Surgery/Medical → CC/MCC → DRG",
      content: `## How Every Case Gets a DRG

The **DRG Grouper** is software that reads coded data and assigns a single MS-DRG through a decision tree:

### Step 1 — Major Diagnostic Category (MDC)
The principal diagnosis maps to one of **25 MDCs** organized by body system.
- Example: MDC 5 = Diseases of the Circulatory System

### Step 2 — Surgery vs. Medical
Was a **significant OR procedure** performed?
- **Yes** → Surgical partition (higher RW)
- **No** → Medical partition

### Step 3 — Complication/Comorbidity Level
Secondary diagnoses are evaluated:
- **MCC** — Major Complication or Comorbidity (highest severity)
- **CC** — Complication or Comorbidity (moderate severity)
- **No CC/MCC** — no significant secondary diagnoses

### Step 4 — Final DRG Assignment
Combining MDC + partition + CC/MCC level produces the **specific MS-DRG number**.

> Not every DRG splits three ways — some split only MCC vs. No CC/MCC, and some don't split at all.`,
