      type: "concept",
      title: "Geometric Mean LOS, Outliers & Two-Midnight Rule",
      content: `## Beyond the Standard Payment

### Geometric Mean Length of Stay (GMLOS)
Each DRG has a GMLOS — the statistical average stay for that group, used for benchmarking, NOT for payment. Payment is fixed regardless of LOS.

- If patient stays **less** than GMLOS → hospital profits (or less loss)
- If patient stays **more** than GMLOS → hospital absorbs extra cost

### Outlier Payments
IPPS includes a safety valve for extremely high-cost cases:

1. Calculate the **fixed-loss threshold** (DRG payment + outlier threshold set by CMS)
2. If a case's **actual cost** exceeds the threshold, Medicare pays an additional **80%** of the excess cost
3. Designed to protect hospitals from catastrophic losses on complex cases

> Outlier payments are estimated to be ~5–6% of total IPPS payments.

### Two-Midnight Rule
Governs whether a stay qualifies for **inpatient** (IPPS) vs. **outpatient** (OPPS) billing:

- **Rule:** A physician must expect the patient to require hospital care spanning **at least two midnights**
- If the expectation exists → admit as inpatient → bill under IPPS
- If not → treat as outpatient observation → bill under OPPS (lower payment)

> This rule was implemented in 2013 to reduce inappropriate inpatient admissions.`,
