      type: "application",
      title: "Applying IPPS Knowledge: Real HIM Scenarios",
      content: `## Where IPPS Knowledge Shows Up in HIM Practice

### 1. Clinical Documentation Integrity (CDI)
CDI specialists review records **before** coding to identify opportunities to query physicians for missing or unclear documentation — especially for CC/MCC capture.

**Your role:** Understand what diagnoses trigger MCC/CC so you can spot gaps or validate CDI queries.

### 2. DRG Validation & Coding Audits
Internal and external auditors compare coded DRGs to clinical documentation. A mismatch can mean:
- **Undercoded** → revenue loss (rebill opportunity)
- **Overcoded** → overpayment, compliance liability, potential False Claims Act exposure

### 3. Outlier Identification
Finance and HIM teams monitor high-cost cases to determine if they qualify for outlier payments. Accurate charge capture is critical — outlier calculation is cost-based.

### 4. Admission Status Review (Two-Midnight)
Case managers and HIM work together to ensure the correct inpatient/outpatient designation. Incorrect status = wrong billing system, potential denial.

### 5. Payer Reporting & MS-DRG Trending
HIM analysts use MS-DRG distribution reports to track case mix index (CMI) over time:
- Falling CMI → possible undercoding or patient population shift
- Rising CMI → higher reimbursement, but may trigger audits

> **Case Mix Index (CMI)** = Average Relative Weight of all cases = measure of hospital complexity and revenue potential.`,
