      content: `## What Is OPPS?

The **Outpatient Prospective Payment System (OPPS)** is Medicare's payment methodology for hospital outpatient services. Implemented in 2000, it replaced cost-based reimbursement with fixed, predetermined payment rates.

### Settings Covered by OPPS
- **Hospital Outpatient Departments (HOPDs)** — clinics, procedure rooms, imaging centers attached to hospitals
- **Ambulatory Surgical Centers (ASCs)** — freestanding facilities for same-day surgeries
- **Emergency Departments (EDs)** — both Level I–V visits

### Why It Matters
Prior to OPPS, hospitals were reimbursed based on actual costs — creating little incentive for efficiency. OPPS pays a **fixed rate per service group**, so hospitals that operate efficiently keep the difference.

> **Key principle:** Medicare pays a predetermined amount regardless of what the service actually costs the hospital.`,
