      content: `## SNF PDPM: Five Payment Components

Effective **October 1, 2019**, CMS replaced the Resource Utilization Group (RUG-IV) system with PDPM for Skilled Nursing Facilities. PDPM is **patient-driven**, basing payment on clinical characteristics rather than therapy minutes.

### The Five PDPM Components

| Component | Basis | Classification Tool |
|-----------|-------|---------------------|
| **PT** (Physical Therapy) | Primary diagnosis, functional score | PT clinical category |
| **OT** (Occupational Therapy) | Primary diagnosis, functional score | OT clinical category |
| **SLP** (Speech-Language Path.) | Cognitive impairment, swallowing | SLP clinical category |
| **Nursing** | Clinical condition complexity | Nursing case-mix group |
| **NTA** (Non-Therapy Ancillary) | Comorbidities, high-cost items | NTA score / comorbidity list |

### Key PDPM Features
- **Variable per diem adjustments**: PT and OT rates adjust over the stay (higher early, lower later)
- **ICD-10-CM diagnosis drives classification** — accurate coding is critical
- **Functional scoring**: Uses Section GG of MDS (Minimum Data Set)
- **No therapy minute thresholds** — ends incentive to over-provide therapy

> 💡 **Coder Note:** The primary diagnosis assigned on the MDS directly determines PT, OT, and SLP case-mix groups. Incorrect diagnosis coding = incorrect payment.`,
