      type: "concept",
      title: "The Three RVU Components",
      content: `## Breaking Down the Relative Value Unit

Every CPT® procedure code carries three RVU components, each measuring a distinct resource category:

### 1. Work RVU (wRVU)
Reflects the **physician's personal effort** — time, technical skill, mental effort, judgment, and stress.
- Largest component for most services (~50-55% of total)
- Example: A complex surgery has much higher wRVU than a brief office visit

### 2. Practice Expense RVU (peRVU)
Covers **overhead costs** to run a practice:
- Clinical staff salaries and benefits
- Medical supplies and drugs
- Medical equipment depreciation
- Office rent and utilities
- **Facility vs. Non-Facility** rates differ — when performed in a hospital (facility), the facility bears overhead, so peRVU is lower

### 3. Malpractice RVU (mpRVU)
Covers **professional liability insurance** premiums.
- Smallest component (~3-5% of total)
- Higher for high-risk specialties (e.g., obstetrics, neurosurgery)

> **Memory tip:** Work = Physician | PE = Practice overhead | MP = Malpractice insurance`,
