      content: `## Welcome to Lesson 11

Outpatient coding relies on three interlocking systems: **CPT**, **HCPCS Level II**, and the **2021 revised E/M guidelines**. Together they describe every procedure, service, supply, and visit performed outside an inpatient hospital stay.

### What You Will Master
- CPT code structure and all three categories
- How to select E/M levels using the new MDM or time-based method
- HCPCS Level II prefix meanings and use cases
- High-yield modifiers that change reimbursement
- Place of Service codes and outpatient sequencing rules

> **Exam tip:** The 2021 E/M overhaul eliminated history and exam as drivers of code level. MDM complexity or total time now determines the level — know both methods cold.`,
