      content: `## High-Yield Modifiers

Modifiers are two-character alphanumeric codes appended to CPT or HCPCS codes to clarify circumstances without changing the code's definition.

### Critical E/M Modifiers

| Modifier | Name | When to Use |
|----------|------|-------------|
| **-25** | Significant, Separately Identifiable E/M | E/M on same day as procedure — E/M must be above and beyond the pre/post-procedure work |
| **-57** | Decision for Surgery | E/M where the decision to perform major surgery was made |

### Procedure Modifiers

| Modifier | Name | When to Use |
|----------|------|-------------|
| **-59** | Distinct Procedural Service | Two procedures not normally billed together; proves they are distinct |
| **-76** | Repeat Procedure, Same Physician | Same procedure repeated same day by same provider |
| **-77** | Repeat Procedure, Different Physician | Same procedure repeated by different provider |
| **-LT / -RT** | Left / Right | Identifies laterality of a bilateral procedure |
| **-50** | Bilateral Procedure | Performed bilaterally during same session |

### Place of Service (POS) Codes

| POS | Setting |
|-----|---------|
| **11** | Office |
| **22** | On-Campus Outpatient Hospital |
| **23** | Emergency Department |
| **12** | Home |
| **21** | Inpatient Hospital |

> **Exam tip:** Modifier -25 is the most-tested modifier. The E/M and procedure must each be medically necessary, and the E/M must be a distinct visit beyond routine pre/post care.`,
