      content: `## National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI)

Developed by CMS to prevent improper payment of procedure pairs that **should not be billed together**.

### Column 1 / Column 2 Logic
| Column | Role | Payment |
|--------|------|---------|
| Column 1 | Comprehensive (primary) code | **Paid** |
| Column 2 | Component (bundled) code | **Denied** (bundled into Col 1) |

### Key Rules
- Column 2 code is considered **included** in the work of Column 1
- Billing both = a NCCI edit violation (claim denied or recouped)
- Edits are updated **quarterly** by CMS

### Common Examples
- CPT **27447** (total knee replacement) bundles **27370** (injection into knee joint) — cannot bill both
- CPT **93306** (echo with Doppler) bundles **93307** (echo without Doppler)
- Surgical approach codes bundled into the primary surgical procedure

### Indicator Values
| Indicator | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| 0 | Codes **never** billable together — no modifier can bypass |
| 1 | Modifier **may** allow separate payment when clinically appropriate |`,
