      title: "Charge Capture Gaps — Missing & Late Charges",
      content: `## Charge Capture: The Revenue Foundation

**Charge capture** is the process of recording every billable service provided to a patient. Gaps in this process directly translate to lost revenue.

### Types of Charge Capture Failures

#### 1. Missing Charges
- Services rendered but **never entered** into the billing system
- Common causes: manual charge entry, verbal orders not documented, supply charges not scanned

#### 2. Late Charges
- Charges submitted **after** the timely filing deadline
- Medicare timely filing: **1 year** from date of service
- Commercial payers: 90–180 days typically
- Late charges → claim denial → permanent revenue loss

#### 3. Under-capture (Related to Unbundling Opposite)
- Billing a lower-level code than what was actually performed
- Failure to capture all components of a complex service

### High-Risk Areas for Charge Gaps
| Department | Common Gap |
|-----------|-----------|
| OR / Procedural | Implants, supply charges not captured |
| ED | Level-of-care escalation not updated |
| Radiology | Contrast charges missing |
| Pharmacy | IV medications not linked to charge |
| Nursing units | Wound care, splinting supplies |

### Prevention Strategies
- Daily charge reconciliation reports
- CDM (Chargemaster) audits
- Interface monitoring between clinical systems and billing
- Charge capture hotlines for staff to report missed charges
- Real-time charge entry (vs. paper-based batch entry)`,
