      type: "example",
      title: "Revenue Integrity Committee — Structure & Role",
      content: `## The Revenue Integrity Committee (RIC)

The **Revenue Integrity Committee** is a cross-functional governance body responsible for overseeing the accuracy, completeness, and compliance of the healthcare revenue cycle.

### Typical Committee Composition
| Role | Representative Function |
|------|------------------------|
| Chief Financial Officer (CFO) | Executive sponsor, financial oversight |
| Director of Revenue Cycle | Operational lead |
| Compliance Officer | Regulatory & audit oversight |
| Coding Manager | Coding accuracy, NCCI/MUE issues |
| Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) | Physician documentation |
| HIM Director | Records, DRG, coding integrity |
| Department Managers | Charge capture from clinical areas |
| IT / EHR Analyst | System integrity, charge interface |

### Key RIC Responsibilities
1. **Review charge capture exceptions** — missing, late, or duplicate charges
2. **Audit coding accuracy** — NCCI, MUEs, unbundling, upcoding patterns
3. **Monitor KPIs** — denial rates, days in A/R, clean claim rate, late charge rate
4. **Approve CDM updates** — chargemaster additions, deletions, price corrections
5. **Coordinate education** — train clinical staff on documentation & charge entry
6. **Investigate payer denials** — identify systemic coding or billing problems
7. **Ensure regulatory compliance** — OIG Work Plan, Medicare/Medicaid requirements

### Meeting Cadence
- **Monthly**: KPI dashboard review, denial trending, late charge reports
- **Quarterly**: NCCI edit table updates, CDM audit results
- **Annually**: Comprehensive compliance program review, policy updates`,
