      type: "concept",
      title: "CARC Codes: Claim Adjustment Reason Codes",
      content: `## CARC — Claim Adjustment Reason Codes

**CARC codes** are standardized codes used on an **EOB/ERA** to explain why a payment was adjusted or denied. They are maintained by the Washington Publishing Company (WPC).

Every line item on an EOB has at minimum one CARC code.

---

### Key CARC Codes to Know

| CARC | Meaning | Denial Type |
|---|---|---|
| **4** | The service is inconsistent with the modifier — contractual adjustment | Coding |
| **16** | Claim/service lacks information or has submission/billing error(s) | Administrative |
| **97** | The benefit for this service is included in the payment/allowance for another service/procedure that has already been adjudicated (bundled) | Coding |
| **181** | Claim spans eligible and ineligible periods of coverage — claim limit exceeded | Administrative/Clinical |
| **29** | The time limit for filing has expired | Administrative |
| **50** | These are non-covered services because this is not deemed a medical necessity | Clinical |

---

### How to Read CARC on an ERA

\`\`\`
CLP*1234567890*2*350.00*0.00*0*MC*P12345
SVC*HC:99213*350.00*0.00
CAS*CO*97*350.00
\`\`\`

- **CAS** = Claim Adjustment Segment
- **CO** = Contractual Obligation (group code)
- **97** = CARC code
- **350.00** = Amount adjusted

> Always look at both CARC **and** RARC together — RARC provides the additional explanation.`,
