      title: "RARC Codes & Denial Rate Calculation",
      content: `## RARC — Remittance Advice Remark Codes

**RARC codes** provide additional explanation supplementing a CARC code. They appear on the EOB/ERA alongside CARC codes.

### Key RARC Codes

| RARC | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **MA130** | Your claim contains incomplete and/or invalid information, and no appeal rights are afforded because the claim is unprocessable. |
| **N519** | Invalid combination of HCPCS modifiers. |
| **N30** | Patient cannot be identified as our insured. |
| **MA01** | If you do not agree with what we approved for these services, you may appeal our decision. |

> **RARC MA130** paired with **CARC 16** = unprocessable claim due to missing/invalid data — not appealable, must correct and resubmit.

---

## Denial Rate Calculation

### Formula
$$\\text{Denial Rate} = \\frac{\\text{Total Denied Claims}}{\\text{Total Claims Submitted}} \\times 100$$

### Example
- Claims submitted in Q1: **2,400**
- Claims denied: **168**
- Denial rate = 168 ÷ 2,400 × 100 = **7%**

### Benchmarks

| Rate | Assessment |
|---|---|
| < 5% | Excellent — industry target |
| 5–10% | Acceptable — monitor trends |
| 10–15% | Concerning — root cause analysis needed |
| > 15% | Critical — immediate intervention required |

### What to Track
- Overall denial rate
- Denial rate **by payer**
- Denial rate **by denial type** (clinical vs. admin vs. coding)
- Denial rate **by service line or provider**`,
