      content: `## Proactive Denial Prevention

The best denial is one that **never happens**. Prevention strategies target each stage of the revenue cycle.

---

### Prevention by Stage

**Front-End (Registration & Scheduling)**
- Verify eligibility and benefits at every visit (real-time eligibility tools)
- Confirm prior authorization requirements before the appointment
- Collect accurate patient demographic data
- Verify correct insurance plan and group number

**Clinical Documentation**
- Train providers on medical necessity documentation requirements
- Ensure documentation supports the diagnosis and procedure codes
- Link diagnosis to services clearly in notes
- Meet LCD/NCD criteria for Medicare services

**Coding**
- Regular coder education on NCCI edits and bundling rules
- Use clearinghouse pre-claim edits to catch errors before submission
- Audit high-volume CPT codes monthly for pattern errors
- Keep up with payer-specific coding guidelines

**Billing & Submission**
- Use electronic claim submission with real-time edits
- Implement a timely filing calendar (track deadlines per payer)
- Clean claims checklist before submission
- Monitor clearinghouse rejection reports daily

---

### Prevention ROI
- **$25–$50** average cost to work a denial (staff time + rework)
- **$5–$10** average cost to prevent a denial (process + technology)
- Prevention ROI: **5:1 to 10:1**

> Build a **denial prevention team meeting** — monthly review of denial trends, root causes, and prevention wins across clinical, coding, and billing departments.`,
