      content: `# Medicare Appeals: Five-Level Process

When Medicare denies a claim, the story isn't over. Federal law guarantees beneficiaries and providers a **structured, five-level appeals process** to challenge adverse coverage and payment decisions.

## Why Appeals Matter
- Medicare denies millions of claims annually — many incorrectly
- **Overturn rates are significant** at every level, especially Levels 1–3
- Knowing the process protects revenue and patient access to care

## The Five Levels at a Glance
| Level | Reviewer | Key Deadline |
|-------|----------|-------------|
| 1 | MAC Redetermination | 120 days to file |
| 2 | QIC Reconsideration | 180 days to file |
| 3 | ALJ Hearing | 60 days to file |
| 4 | Medicare Appeals Council | 60 days to file |
| 5 | Federal District Court | 60 days to file |

Each level has **strict filing deadlines** and **dollar thresholds** at the higher levels. Missing a deadline can forfeit your appeal rights entirely.`,
