      type: "quiz",
      title: "Quiz: Filing Deadlines",
      content: `# Quiz: Filing Deadlines

## Question
A hospital receives a Medicare denial notice from the MAC on **March 1**. They file a Level 1 Redetermination request, which the MAC also denies. They receive the MAC's redetermination decision on **May 15**.

**What is the LAST DATE the hospital can file a Level 2 QIC Reconsideration request?**

- A) July 15 (60 days after the Level 1 decision)
- B) November 11 (180 days after the Level 1 decision)
- C) August 28 (180 days after the original March 1 denial)
- D) July 14 (60 days after the original March 1 denial)

---

## Answer: **B) November 11**

### Explanation

The Level 2 QIC filing deadline is **180 days from the date of the MAC redetermination decision** — NOT from the original denial.

**Calculation:**
- MAC redetermination decision date: **May 15**
- Add 180 days: May 15 + 180 days = **November 11**

### Why the Other Answers Are Wrong
| Option | Why Incorrect |
|--------|--------------|
| A (July 15) | 60 days is the MAC's timeframe to DECIDE — not your filing deadline |
| C (August 28) | 180 days from the ORIGINAL denial — but Level 2 clock starts from Level 1 decision |
| D (July 14) | 60 days from original denial — this is not a real filing window |

### Key Rule to Remember
> **Each level's filing deadline starts from the PREVIOUS level's decision date — not from the original denial.**

| Level | Deadline | Starts From |
|-------|----------|-------------|
| Level 1 | 120 days | Original denial notice |
| Level 2 | 180 days | MAC redetermination decision |
| Level 3 | 60 days | QIC reconsideration decision |
| Level 4 | 60 days | ALJ decision |
| Level 5 | 60 days | Appeals Council decision |`,
