      type: "concept",
      title: "Reimbursement Methodology Types",
      content: `## How Payers Reimburse Providers

The reimbursement methodology determines how much a provider is paid and who bears financial risk.

| Methodology | Description | Risk Bearer |
|---|---|---|
| **Fee Schedule** | Fixed payment per service/procedure (e.g., Medicare RBRVS) | Payer (if rates are adequate) |
| **% of Charges** | Payer pays a percentage of the provider's billed charges | Payer |
| **Per Diem** | Flat daily rate regardless of services rendered | Provider (for high-cost days) |
| **Case Rate** | Single bundled payment for an episode of care | Provider |
| **Capitation** | Fixed PMPM payment per enrolled member regardless of utilization | Provider |

**Risk Spectrum:**
- Fee Schedule → % of Charges → Per Diem → Case Rate → **Capitation** (highest provider risk)

**Key insight:** As risk shifts to the provider, the provider has a stronger incentive to manage utilization and costs efficiently.`,
