      type: "concept",
      title: "Network Adequacy & Contract Monitoring KPIs",
      content: `## Ensuring Access and Tracking Performance

### Network Adequacy Standards
Payers must maintain networks that provide **adequate access** to care. Regulatory standards (CMS, state insurance departments) define minimum requirements.

**Key adequacy measures:**
- **Provider-to-member ratios** (e.g., 1 PCP per 1,500–2,000 members)
- **Geographic access** (e.g., 90% of members within 30 miles of a PCP)
- **Specialty access** (e.g., oncologist within 60 miles for 80% of members)
- **Timely access** (routine: 30 days, urgent: 48 hours, emergent: immediate)
- **24/7 access** to on-call provider or nurse triage line

### Contract Monitoring KPIs

| KPI | Definition | Target |
|---|---|---|
| **Payment Accuracy Rate** | % of claims paid at contracted rate | ≥ 98% |
| **Timely Payment Rate** | % of clean claims paid within contract timeframe | ≥ 95% |
| **Underpayment Rate** | % of claims paid below contracted amount | < 2% |
| **Denial Rate** | % of submitted claims denied | < 5% |
| **Clean Claim Rate** | % of claims requiring no correction on first submission | ≥ 95% |

### Managed Care Contract Audit
- **Frequency**: Annual audit recommended; quarterly for high-volume payers
- **Process**: Compare EOB payment amounts to contracted fee schedule line by line
- **Findings**: Underpayments, miscoded rates, non-standard write-offs
- **Recovery**: File corrected claims or dispute requests within contract timeframe`,
