      title: "Quiz: Reimbursement Methodology Matching",
      content: `A hospital receives a fixed payment of $6,500 for every knee replacement surgery, regardless of how many days the patient stays or what supplies are used. Which reimbursement methodology does this describe?

A. Fee-for-service (percentage of charges)
B. Per diem rate
C. Case rate (bundled payment)
D. Capitation (PMPM)

---

**Answer: C**

**Explanation:**
A case rate (bundled payment) is a single fixed payment that covers an entire episode of care — in this case, the full knee replacement regardless of LOS or resource use. The provider profits if costs are below $6,500 and loses if costs exceed it. Per diem pays per day of stay; fee-for-service pays per individual service billed; capitation pays per enrolled member per month regardless of whether services are used.`,
