      content: `## Why Compliance Matters in HIM\n\nCoding professionals sit at the intersection of clinical documentation and financial reimbursement. Every code assigned translates into a payment — and the gap between legitimate coding and **fraudulent billing** can mean millions in federal penalties.\n\n### Revenue Integrity vs. Fraud\n| Revenue Integrity | Fraud |\n|---|---|\n| Capture all documented diagnoses | Assign diagnoses documentation doesn't support |\n| Physician queries for clarification | Change codes based on financial pressure |\n| CDI-driven CMI improvement | Systematic upcoding to higher DRGs |\n| Complete accurate code sets | Phantom charges, duplicate billing |\n\n### The Stakes\n- **False Claims Act** civil penalties: $13,946–$27,894 *per claim* (FY2024)\n- **OIG exclusion** from Medicare/Medicaid programs\n- **Individual criminal liability** for HIM professionals\n- **Corporate integrity agreements** costing millions\n\n> A coder who assigns a code knowing it is not supported by documentation is not just making an error — they may be committing fraud.`,
