      content: `## Welcome to Lesson 22

**Medicare Advantage (MA)** — also called **Part C** — allows beneficiaries to receive Medicare benefits through private health plans instead of traditional fee-for-service Medicare.

### What You'll Learn
- How MA plans are structured and funded through **capitation payments**
- The role of **Risk Adjustment Factor (RAF)** scores in determining plan revenue
- How CMS validates risk coding accuracy through **RADV audits**
- The difference between **prospective** and **retrospective** chart review
- Documentation best practices at **Annual Wellness Visits (AWV)**

> **Why It Matters:** Accurate HCC capture directly determines how much MA plans are paid. Inaccurate coding triggers federal audits and repayment demands.`,
