      content: `## Part C: Medicare Advantage

Medicare Advantage (MA) is the **private-plan alternative** to traditional Medicare (Parts A & B).

### Key Features
| Feature | Traditional Medicare | Medicare Advantage |
|---|---|---|
| Administered by | CMS directly | Private insurers |
| Payment model | Fee-for-service | Capitation (PMPM) |
| Network | Any Medicare provider | Plan network |
| Extra benefits | None | Dental, vision, etc. |
| Risk to plan | None | Plan bears risk |

### Plan Types
- **HMO** — requires referrals, in-network only
- **PPO** — allows out-of-network at higher cost
- **PFFS** — plan sets payment terms; any willing provider
- **SNP (Special Needs Plans)** — target specific populations (dual-eligible, chronic conditions, institutionalized)

### How Plans Are Paid
CMS pays each MA plan a **monthly capitation payment** per enrollee. The amount is determined by:
1. A **base rate** (benchmark) for the county
2. Adjusted by the enrollee's **RAF score** (Risk Adjustment Factor)

> **Formula:** Payment = Base Rate × RAF Score`,
