      type: "quiz",
      title: "Quiz: AWV Documentation Requirements",
      content: `## Quiz Question 2

A physician sees an MA enrollee for her Annual Wellness Visit. The patient has the following conditions documented in last year's records:
- Type 2 diabetes mellitus, uncontrolled (HCC 19)
- Major depressive disorder, recurrent, moderate (HCC 59)
- Peripheral artery disease (HCC 108)

The physician's AWV note today reads:
> *"Patient doing well. Reviewed medications. No acute complaints. Continue current management. Schedule follow-up in 6 months."*
>
> *Codes submitted: G0439*

**Question:** Which of the following statements is MOST accurate regarding this AWV encounter?

**A)** All three HCCs are captured because the patient was seen and G0439 was billed.

**B)** The HCCs will automatically carry forward from last year without re-documentation.

**C)** None of the three HCCs are captured for this contract year from this encounter.

**D)** Only HCC 19 (diabetes) is captured because it was uncontrolled last year.

---

**Correct Answer: C) None of the three HCCs are captured for this contract year from this encounter.**

### Explanation

**Why C is correct:**
The physician documented only that the patient is "doing well" with no new complaints — but **failed to specifically assess and document each active chronic condition**. HCC capture requires that:
1. The diagnosis is **explicitly documented** in the assessment/plan
2. An **ICD-10 code** is submitted for the specific condition
3. This happens at least **once per calendar year**

The note contains no mention of diabetes, depression, or PAD — therefore no HCC codes can be submitted from this encounter.

**Why not A?** Billing G0439 alone does not capture HCCs — diagnoses must be individually documented and coded.

**Why not B?** HCCs **never carry forward automatically**. They expire at year-end if not recaptured.

**Why not D?** "Uncontrolled" status from last year has no bearing on this year's documentation — the condition must be re-assessed and documented again.

> **Rule to remember:** If it's not documented, it's not coded. If it's not coded, there is no HCC. If there's no HCC, there's no RAF credit.`,
