      content: `## MSSP Structure

The **Medicare Shared Savings Program** allows groups of providers to form an **Accountable Care Organization (ACO)** to coordinate care for Medicare FFS beneficiaries.

### ACO Tracks

#### Basic Track (Levels A–E)
- **Levels A & B**: Upside only — share savings, no loss risk
- **Levels C, D, E**: Graduated two-sided risk
- Entry point for new ACOs
- Lower shared savings rate (up to 40%)

#### Enhanced Track
- **Two-sided risk from day one**
- Higher shared savings rate (up to **75%**)
- Qualifies as Advanced APM (higher Medicare bonuses)
- Access to advance infrastructure payments

### Key MSSP Features
| Feature | Detail |
|---------|--------|
| Minimum savings rate (MSR) | Must beat benchmark by 2–3.9% to qualify |
| Benchmark | 3-year historical spending, risk-adjusted |
| Agreement period | 5 years |
| Quality gate | Must meet quality performance threshold to share savings |
| Attribution | Claims-based (plurality of primary care visits) |

### HIM Impact
- **Risk adjustment**: HCC codes from all providers in the ACO roll up to set the benchmark
- **Missing diagnoses** = artificially low benchmark = harder to show savings`,
