      type: "concept",
      title: "Primary Care Models: PCF & ACO REACH",
      content: `## Advanced Primary Care APMs

Beyond MSSP, CMS has created primary care-focused models that go further in transforming payment.

### Primary Care First (PCF)
- **Target**: Small/medium primary care practices
- **Structure**: Enhanced fee schedule + performance-based adjustments
- **Focus**: Reducing hospitalizations from primary care settings
- **Risk**: Downside risk tied to hospital utilization rates
- **Coding impact**: Accurate chronic disease coding affects risk payments

### ACO REACH (Realizing Equity, Access, and Community Health)
Previously called "Direct Contracting Entity (DCE)"
- **Full/Partial Capitation**: Provider receives a per-member-per-month payment
- **Population**: Medicare FFS beneficiaries attributed to the ACO
- **Three entity types**:
  | Type | Description |
  |------|-------------|
  | Professional | Physician-led, 50% risk |
  | Global | Full capitation, 100% risk |
  | High Needs | Complex/chronically ill populations |
- **Equity focus**: Required health equity plans, data collection on social needs

### Why ACO REACH is Different
- **Most advanced** APM available
- Practices must have infrastructure for population health
- **HCC coding critical**: Per-member payment is risk-adjusted monthly
- Missing HCCs = underpayment every month for that patient

### Key Comparison
| | MSSP | BPCI Advanced | ACO REACH |
|--|------|------|------|
| Payment basis | Shared savings | Episode bundle | Capitation |
| Risk level | Low → High | Two-sided | High |
| Time horizon | Annual | 90-day episode | Ongoing monthly |
| HCC importance | High | Medium | Very High |`,
