      title: "HIM's Role in Population Health Management",
      content: `## From Individual Encounters to Population Health

HIM professionals are no longer just coders — in the APM era, they are **population health data stewards**.

### The HIM-Population Health Connection

#### 1. HCC Capture & Risk Scoring
- Every chronic condition documented and coded contributes to **CMS-HCC risk scores**
- Risk scores drive benchmark setting in MSSP and capitation rates in ACO REACH
- **Annual recapture required**: chronic conditions must be coded every year they are active
- HIM role: query providers for missing diagnoses, audit for completeness

#### 2. Episode Attribution Accuracy
- In BPCI, the **principal diagnosis code** determines which episode type applies
- Wrong principal dx → wrong bundle → incorrect financial accountability
- HIM role: ensure PDx follows UHDDS guidelines, query when needed

#### 3. Quality Measure Data Integrity
- Quality measures often rely on coded diagnoses (e.g., diabetes dx for HbA1c measure denominator)
- **Documentation gaps** cause patients to fall out of quality measure numerators
- HIM role: close documentation gaps through CDI programs

#### 4. Utilization Analysis
- APM administrators analyze claims data for utilization patterns
- Coding must reflect actual resource use (LOS, procedures, complications)
- HIM role: ensure coding supports accurate utilization reporting

### Practical CDI Strategies for APMs
| Strategy | Impact |
|----------|--------|
| Annual wellness visit HCC capture | Raises benchmark |
| Post-discharge coding audits | Catches missed CCs for BPCI |
| Chronic disease status queries | Ensures quality measure accuracy |
| Risk score trending reports | Identifies coding gaps by provider |`,
