      type: "example",
      title: "HIM Career Pathways — CCA to RHIA and Specializations",
      content: `# HIM Career Pathways

## The Credential Ladder

### Entry Level — CCA (Certified Coding Associate)
- **Issuer**: AHIMA
- **Eligibility**: No experience required; high school diploma or equivalent
- **Exam focus**: ICD-10-CM, CPT, medical terminology, compliance basics
- **Role**: Outpatient/physician office coder, entry-level HIM positions
- **Salary range**: $38,000–$52,000

### Mid Level — CCS (Certified Coding Specialist)
- **Issuer**: AHIMA
- **Eligibility**: Work experience recommended; no degree requirement
- **Exam focus**: Complex inpatient coding, DRG assignment, ICD-10-PCS, APC
- **Role**: Hospital inpatient coder, coding auditor, compliance specialist
- **Salary range**: $52,000–$72,000

### Advanced Level — RHIA (Registered Health Information Administrator)
- **Issuer**: AHIMA
- **Eligibility**: Accredited HIM bachelor's degree (or AHIMA bridge pathway)
- **Exam focus**: HIM management, data analytics, privacy, healthcare operations
- **Role**: HIM director, compliance officer, CDI manager, data governance
- **Salary range**: $65,000–$110,000+

---

## Specialty Credentials

### CDIP (Certified Documentation Improvement Practitioner)
- Focus: Clinical Documentation Integrity — working with physicians to improve documentation quality
- Target: CDI specialists, utilization review, case management

### CRC (Certified Risk Adjustment Coder)
- Focus: HCC (Hierarchical Condition Category) coding for Medicare Advantage and ACA risk adjustment
- Target: Value-based care organizations, managed care plans, ACOs

### CHDA (Certified Health Data Analyst)
- Focus: Health data analysis, data quality, reporting
- Target: Data analysts, population health roles

---

## Career Pivot Points
\`\`\`
CCA → CCS: 1-2 years inpatient coding experience
CCS → RHIA: HIM bachelor's degree + leadership experience
CCS → CDIP: CDI training + clinical documentation focus
CCS → CRC: Risk adjustment training + managed care exposure
\`\`\``,
