      type: "concept",
      title: "Key Healthcare Data Users",
      content: `## Who Uses Healthcare Statistics — and Why?

Healthcare data serves a wide ecosystem of stakeholders. HIM professionals must understand each user's needs because they shape **what data is collected**, **how it's reported**, and **what privacy protections apply**.

---

### Hospital Administration & Leadership
- **Uses**: Operating metrics, bed utilization, staffing ratios, financial performance
- **Key stats**: Average length of stay (ALOS), occupancy rate, case mix index (CMI)
- **Goal**: Maximize efficiency and financial sustainability

### Physicians & Clinical Staff
- **Uses**: Outcome benchmarks, readmission rates, complication rates, clinical protocols
- **Key stats**: Infection rates, surgical complication rates, mortality by diagnosis
- **Goal**: Improve clinical quality and patient safety

### Payers (Insurance Companies, CMS)
- **Uses**: Reimbursement validation, fraud detection, utilization review
- **Key stats**: DRG assignment accuracy, procedure codes, length of stay vs. benchmark
- **Goal**: Ensure appropriate payment for services rendered

### Government & Regulatory Bodies
- **Uses**: Public health surveillance, policy development, mandatory reporting
- **Key stats**: Communicable disease rates, vital statistics, hospital-acquired conditions
- **Goal**: Protect population health and enforce standards

### Researchers & Epidemiologists
- **Uses**: Disease causation studies, treatment effectiveness trials, population trends
- **Key stats**: Incidence rates, prevalence rates, relative risk, odds ratios
- **Goal**: Generate new knowledge to advance medicine

### Accreditation Bodies (Joint Commission, DNV, HFAP)
- **Uses**: Compliance with quality standards, patient safety metrics
- **Key stats**: Core measures, never events, sentinel event rates
- **Goal**: Ensure facilities meet minimum safety and quality thresholds

---

> HIM professionals must tailor **data presentation** to each user — a physician reads raw rates differently than an administrator reads a dashboard.`,
