      type: "application",
      title: "Applying Healthcare Statistics: A Day in the Life",
      content: `## Real-World Application: Morning Statistics Report

You are the HIM analyst at Riverside Community Hospital. It's Monday morning and you need to prepare the **weekly statistics report** for the administrative committee meeting.

---

### Your Data for the Week (Monday–Sunday)

| Day | Admissions | Discharges | Patient Days | Deaths |
|-----|-----------|-----------|--------------|--------|
| Mon | 24 | 19 | 187 | 1 |
| Tue | 31 | 28 | 192 | 0 |
| Wed | 22 | 25 | 189 | 2 |
| Thu | 28 | 30 | 195 | 1 |
| Fri | 35 | 22 | 201 | 0 |
| Sat | 18 | 24 | 198 | 1 |
| Sun | 15 | 20 | 190 | 0 |
| **Total** | **173** | **168** | **1,352** | **5** |

---

### Calculate These Statistics

**1. Gross Death Rate (GDR)**
$$\\text{GDR} = \\frac{\\text{Total Deaths}}{\\text{Total Discharges (including deaths)}} \\times 100$$
$$= \\frac{5}{168} \\times 100 = 2.98\\%$$

**2. Average Length of Stay (ALOS)**
- Total discharge days needed (assume 975 total discharge days for the week)
$$\\text{ALOS} = \\frac{\\text{Total Discharge Days}}{\\text{Total Discharges}} = \\frac{975}{168} = 5.8 \\text{ days}$$

**3. Average Daily Census (ADC)**
$$\\text{ADC} = \\frac{\\text{Total Inpatient Service Days}}{\\text{Number of Days in Period}} = \\frac{1{,}352}{7} = 193.1 \\text{ patients/day}$$

---

### How to Present This

- **For physicians**: GDR above 2% flagged for mortality review committee
- **For administration**: ADC of 193 vs. licensed bed capacity determines staffing needs
- **For compliance**: Report deaths meeting certain criteria to medical examiner
- **For accreditation**: Track against prior months for trend analysis

> Every number tells a story. The HIM analyst's job is to make sure the right people hear the right story at the right time.`,
