      title: "Hospital Death Rates: Why They Matter",
      content: "Hospital death rates are among the most closely watched quality indicators in healthcare. Regulators, accreditation bodies (like The Joint Commission), payers, and the public use death rates to benchmark hospital performance, guide resource allocation, and identify opportunities for quality improvement.\n\nA single facility may track multiple death rates — each designed to isolate a different aspect of care. In this lesson you will learn the formulas, the numerators and denominators that define each rate, and the reasoning behind key distinctions (such as why deaths within 48 hours are separated out).\n\n**Rates covered in this lesson:**\n- Gross death rate\n- Net death rate (institutional death rate)\n- Postoperative death rate\n- Anesthesia death rate\n- Newborn death rate\n- Fetal (stillbirth) death rate\n- Maternal death rate",
