      title: "Obstetric & Newborn Statistics",
      content: "Obstetric and newborn statistics measure the outcomes of pregnancy, delivery, and the immediate newborn period. Health information professionals track these rates to support quality improvement, benchmark performance, and meet reporting requirements. Key metrics include fetal death rates, newborn death rates, maternal death rates, cesarean section rates, and VBAC rates. Newborn patient data is always counted and reported **separately** from adult and pediatric data — a critical distinction in health care statistics.",
