      title: "Outpatient & Ambulatory Statistics",
      content: "Outpatient care represents the fastest-growing segment of healthcare delivery. An **outpatient** is a patient who receives professional services without a formal inpatient admission — they do not occupy a hospital bed overnight for treatment purposes.\n\nOutpatient settings include:\n- **Clinic visits** (primary care, specialty)\n- **Emergency department (ED) visits**\n- **Observation status** patients\n- **Same-day (ambulatory) surgery**\n- **Ancillary services** — lab draws, radiology scans, physical therapy\n\nHealth information professionals must track outpatient statistics separately from inpatient data. The data sources, billing forms, payment systems, and quality measures are all distinct. Mastering outpatient statistics is essential for coding, compliance, revenue cycle, and quality reporting roles.",
