      type: "concept",
      title: "Six Dimensions of Data Quality",
      content: `# Six Dimensions of Data Quality

Use the mnemonic **ACCCRG** to remember all six:

| Dimension | Definition | Example |
|-----------|-----------|---------|
| **A**ccuracy | Data is correct and error-free | DOB entered as 1986, not 1968 |
| **C**ompleteness | All required fields are present | Discharge summary signed before record closes |
| **C**onsistency | Data matches across all documents | Diagnosis in H&P matches discharge summary |
| **C**urrency | Data is up-to-date and timely | Allergy list reviewed at each visit |
| **R**elevance | Data is meaningful for its purpose | Only pertinent history documented |
| **G**ranularity | Appropriate level of detail | "Fracture of left distal radius" not just "arm injury" |

> **Mnemonic:** **A** **C**lean **C**hart **C**orrectly **R**ecords every **G**ranular detail.

Each dimension can be monitored through audits and is tied to accreditation standards.`,
