      type: "example",
      title: "Deficiency Analysis Example",
      content: `# Deficiency Analysis Example

A hospital HIM department conducts a monthly audit of 50 randomly selected discharged records.

**Audit Results:**

| Deficiency Type | Records Affected | Percentage |
|----------------|-----------------|-----------|
| Unsigned H&P | 8 | 16% |
| Missing discharge summary | 5 | 10% |
| Operative report late | 3 | 6% |
| Co-signature missing | 4 | 8% |
| No deficiency | 30 | 60% |

**Step 1: Calculate deficiency rate**
> Records with any deficiency: 50 − 30 = **20 records**
> Deficiency rate = 20 ÷ 50 = **40%**

**Step 2: Identify the top problem**
> Unsigned H&P = 16% → Focus education on attending physicians

**Step 3: Recommend action**
- Send targeted notices to physicians with unsigned H&Ps
- Set 7-day completion reminder in EHR
- Report to Medical Records Committee next meeting

**Step 4: Follow-up audit**
- Re-audit next month to measure improvement
- Goal: Reduce deficiency rate below 20%

> This structured approach turns data into actionable quality improvement.`,
