      title: "HIM Scenario: Annual Quality Audit",
      content: `# HIM Scenario: Annual Quality Audit

You are the HIM manager at a 250-bed hospital. Your director asks you to lead the annual data quality audit. Here is what you find from a 100-chart sample:

**Audit Findings:**

| Issue | Count |
|-------|-------|
| Missing discharge summaries | 14 |
| Unsigned physician orders | 9 |
| Coding errors (ICD-10 specificity) | 11 |
| MPI duplicates identified | 6 |
| Records with no deficiency | 60 |

**Step 1: Calculate deficiency rate**
Records with any deficiency: 100 − 60 = 40
**Deficiency Rate = 40%**

**Step 2: Prioritize issues**
1. Missing discharge summaries (14) — highest volume, billing impact
2. Coding errors (11) — revenue and compliance risk
3. Unsigned orders (9) — patient safety and legal risk

**Step 3: Draft your improvement plan**
- Discharge summaries: Set 48-hour dictation reminder in EHR; report to department chairs
- Coding: Schedule ICD-10 specificity training with coding staff; CDI query process
- MPI: Initiate MPI cleanup project; assign data steward to monitor duplicates monthly

**Step 4: PDSA**
- Plan: Each intervention above
- Do: Implement over next 60 days
- Study: Re-audit 100 charts at 60 days
- Act: Standardize what works; revise what doesn't

**Goal:** Reduce deficiency rate from 40% to below 15% within 90 days.`,
