      type: "concept",
      title: "Specialty Death Rates (L5)",
      content: `# Specialty Death Rates

All specialty death rates use ×100 as the multiplier unless otherwise noted.

## Postoperative (Postop) Death Rate
> (Deaths within 10 days of surgery ÷ Patients who had surgery) × 100

## Newborn Death Rate
> (Newborn deaths ÷ NB discharges including NB deaths) × 100

## Fetal Death Rate
> (Intermediate + late fetal deaths ÷ (Total births + intermediate + late fetal deaths)) × 100

## Maternal Death Rate (Direct)
> (Direct maternal deaths ÷ Total obstetric discharges including maternal deaths) × 100

---

## Fetal Death Classifications

| Term | Gestational Age |
|------|----------------|
| Early | < 20 weeks |
| Intermediate | 20–27 weeks |
| Late | ≥ 28 weeks |

Only **intermediate** and **late** fetal deaths are included in the fetal death rate denominator.`,
