      title: "HAI & Surgical Rates (L7–L8)",
      content: `# HAI & Surgical Rates

## Hospital-Acquired Infection (HAI) Rate
> (HAI cases ÷ Total discharges) × 100

Also called the nosocomial infection rate. Only infections **acquired during the hospitalization** count.

---

## Postoperative Infection Rate
> (Postop infections ÷ Patients who had surgery) × 100

---

## Anesthesia Death Rate
> (Anesthesia deaths ÷ Patients who had anesthesia) × 100

---

## Operating Room (OR) Utilization Rate
> (Actual OR hours used ÷ Available OR hours) × 100

---

## Key Distinctions

| Term | Means |
|------|-------|
| HAI | Infection acquired IN the hospital |
| Community-acquired | Infection the patient arrived WITH |
| Postop infection | Specifically after a surgical procedure |

**Exam trap:** An infection the patient had before admission is NOT an HAI. Only count infections that developed after admission.`,
