      type: "concept",
      title: "Vital Statistics (L13)",
      content: `# Vital Statistics

Vital statistics measure population-level health events. The multiplier is 1,000 or 100,000 — NOT 100.

## Birth Rate (Crude)
> (Total live births / Mid-year population) x 1,000

## Infant Mortality Rate
> (Deaths under age 1 / Live births in same year) x 1,000

## Crude Death Rate
> (Total deaths / Mid-year population) x 1,000

## Cause-Specific Death Rate
> (Deaths from specific cause / Mid-year population) x 100,000

## Case Fatality Rate
> (Deaths from disease / Cases of that disease) x 100

---

## Multiplier Reference

| Rate | Multiplier |
|------|-----------|
| Birth rate | x 1,000 |
| Infant mortality | x 1,000 |
| Crude death rate | x 1,000 |
| Cause-specific death | x 100,000 |
| Case fatality | x 100 |

**Exam trap:** Birth and crude death rates use x1,000 — never x100.`,
