      type: "concept",
      title: "Performance Metrics (L14)",
      content: `# Performance Metrics

## Case Mix Index (CMI)
Measures the relative complexity of the hospital's patient population.

> CMI = Sum of DRG weights / Total discharges

Higher CMI = more complex patients = higher reimbursement.

## HCAHPS
Hospital Consumer Assessment of Healthcare Providers and Systems. Standardized patient satisfaction survey. Results are publicly reported and affect reimbursement.

Key domains: nurse and doctor communication, staff responsiveness, cleanliness, pain management, discharge information, overall rating.

## Dashboard KPIs

| KPI | Measures |
|-----|---------|
| 30-day readmission rate | Patients returning within 30 days |
| Average LOS | Efficiency |
| Bed occupancy | Capacity use |
| Mortality rate | Quality outcome |
| HCAHPS score | Patient satisfaction |
| CMI | Patient complexity |

**Key point:** Always adjust for CMI before comparing mortality rates across different hospitals.`,
