      content: `A hospital had 40 deaths. Of those, 3 cases were referred to the medical examiner/coroner. The hospital performed 12 autopsies. What is the net autopsy rate?

A. 12/40 x 100 = 30.0%
B. 12/43 x 100 = 27.9%
C. 12/(40-3) x 100 = 32.4%
D. (12-3)/40 x 100 = 22.5%

---

**Answer: C**

**Explanation:**
The net autopsy rate removes ME/coroner cases from the denominator because those bodies are unavailable to the hospital.

- Numerator: 12 hospital autopsies (unchanged)
- Denominator: 40 deaths - 3 ME/coroner cases = 37
- Net Autopsy Rate = 12/37 x 100 = **32.4%**

ME/coroner cases come out of the denominator only, not the numerator. Option D incorrectly subtracts from the numerator. Option A is the gross rate (no ME/coroner adjustment).`,
