      content: `A hospital had 250 total deliveries during the month. Of those, 75 were cesarean sections. What is the C-section rate?

A. 250/75 x 100 = 333%
B. 75/250 x 100 = 30%
C. 75/(250-75) x 100 = 42.9%
D. 75/250 = 0.30

---

**Answer: B**

**Explanation:**
C-section rate = (C-section deliveries / Total deliveries) x 100

= 75/250 x 100 = **30%**

This means 30% of all deliveries were cesarean sections. The denominator is total deliveries (not total patients or total births). Option D has the correct calculation but is missing the x100 multiplier — the answer must be expressed as a percentage. Option C incorrectly subtracts C-sections from the denominator.`,
