      type: "concept",
      title: "NB & Fetal Autopsy Rates + HAI Rates",
      content: `# Newborn & Fetal Autopsy Rates + Infection Rates

## Newborn Autopsy Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
NB Autopsy Rate = (NB Autopsies / NB Deaths) × 100
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "Baby autopsies over baby deaths — simple!"

---

## Fetal Autopsy Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
Fetal Autopsy Rate = (Fetal Autopsies / Fetal Deaths) × 100
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "Fetal autopsies over fetal deaths — not births, just deaths"

---

## HAI (Nosocomial Infection) Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
HAI Rate = (Patients with HAI / Total Discharges) × 100
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "HAI = Hospital-Acquired Infections over all Discharges"

HAI = Healthcare-Associated Infection = Nosocomial Infection (same thing, different terms)

---

## Postoperative Infection Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
Postop Infection Rate = (Postop Wound Infections / Surgeries Performed) × 100
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "Wound infections over wound-makers (surgeries)"

---

## Worked Example
Data: 200 discharges | 8 HAI patients | 50 surgeries | 3 postop wound infections | 5 NB deaths | 4 NB autopsies

- **HAI Rate:** (8/200) × 100 = **4.0%**
- **Postop Infection:** (3/50) × 100 = **6.0%**
- **NB Autopsy:** (4/5) × 100 = **80.0%**

---

## Key Distinction
| Rate | Numerator | Denominator |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| HAI rate | HAI patients | All discharges |
| Postop infection | Wound infections | Surgeries only |`,
