      type: "concept",
      title: "Vital Statistics: Mortality Rates",
      content: `# Vital Statistics — Mortality Rates

All use **live births** as denominator (not midyear population)!

## Infant Mortality Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
Infant Mortality Rate = (Deaths <1 year / Live Births) × 1,000
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "Infant = under one, over births × 1K"

---

## Neonatal Mortality Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
Neonatal Mortality Rate = (Deaths <28 days / Live Births) × 1,000
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "NEO = New life under 28 days"
*(First 4 weeks = neonatal period)*

---

## Postneonatal Mortality Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
Postneonatal = (Deaths 28 days to <1 year / Live Births) × 1,000
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "POST-neo = After 28 days but still under 1 year"

---

## Maternal Mortality Rate
**Formula:**
\`\`\`
Maternal Mortality Rate = (Maternal Deaths / Live Births) × 100,000
\`\`\`
**Mnemonic:** "MOM = Maternal Over Maternity × 100K" (rare — needs 100,000 multiplier)

**Note:** This is the VITAL STATISTICS version. The hospital version uses obstetric discharges × 100.

---

## Worked Example
Live births: 2,000 | Deaths <1 yr: 16 | Deaths <28 days: 10 | Deaths 28d−<1yr: 6 | Maternal deaths: 1

- **Infant:** (16/2,000) × 1,000 = **8.0 per 1,000**
- **Neonatal:** (10/2,000) × 1,000 = **5.0 per 1,000**
- **Postneonatal:** (6/2,000) × 1,000 = **3.0 per 1,000**
- **Maternal:** (1/2,000) × 100,000 = **50.0 per 100,000**

*Check:* Infant = Neonatal + Postneonatal (8 = 5 + 3 ✓)`,
