      title: "Quiz 5: Mixed Formula Challenge",
      content: `An OB unit had 200 total deliveries: 180 live births and 20 fetal deaths. 60 deliveries were C-sections. There were 2 maternal deaths. The unit had 4 postoperative deaths from 50 surgeries.

Calculate:
1. Fetal death rate
2. C-section rate
3. Maternal death rate (hospital version)
4. Postoperative death rate

A. Fetal: 10% | C-sec: 33.3% | Maternal: 1.1% | Postop: 8%
B. Fetal: 11.1% | C-sec: 30% | Maternal: 1.0% | Postop: 8%
C. Fetal: 10% | C-sec: 30% | Maternal: 1.0% | Postop: 8%
D. Fetal: 10% | C-sec: 30% | Maternal: 1.1% | Postop: 8%

---

**Answer: D**

**Explanation:**
1. **Fetal death rate:** Fetal deaths / (live births + fetal deaths) × 100
   = 20 / (180 + 20) × 100 = 20/200 × 100 = **10.0%**

2. **C-section rate:** C-sections / total deliveries × 100
   = 60 / 200 × 100 = **30.0%**

3. **Maternal death rate (hospital):** Maternal deaths / obstetric discharges × 100
   = 2 / 200 × 100 = **1.0%**

4. **Postop death rate:** Postop deaths / surgeries performed × 100
   = 4 / 50 × 100 = **8.0%**

Option D matches all four. Option A gets C-section wrong (uses live births not total deliveries). Option B gets fetal wrong (uses only live births as denominator).`,
