      content: "The health record is the primary source of patient data -- but the healthcare system runs on SECONDARY data derived from those records. Data sets standardize what information is collected. Registries aggregate data for surveillance, research, and quality improvement. Indices allow you to locate records and track patterns. This lesson covers all the major data sets (UHDDS, UACDS, MDS, OASIS, IRF-PAI, DEEDS, HEDIS), the registry systems (cancer, trauma, birth defect, transplant, immunization), and the indices that HIM professionals maintain. Domain 1 subtask 1.6 specifically tests your ability to 'manage secondary data sources' -- and these concepts also appear in Domain 3 (analytics) and Domain 4 (reimbursement) questions. If a question mentions a specific care setting, you MUST know which data set applies. This is pure memorization territory -- and the exam WILL test it.",
