        content: "This lesson covers the four major health record formats (source-oriented, problem-oriented, integrated, and hybrid), paper-based record processes including chart assembly and analysis, EHR documentation practices and risks, and record retention and destruction requirements. These topics fall under RHIT Domain 1, Subtasks 1.1 and 1.3, and represent approximately 22% of the exam. Understanding the differences between record formats and between quantitative and qualitative analysis is high-yield material that appears on virtually every RHIT exam.",
        visual: { type: "diagram", svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" class="lesson-visual"><rect x="0" y="0" width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" font-size="42" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Health Record Formats</text><text x="550" y="100" font-size="29" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">Domain 1 | Subtasks 1.1, 1.3 | 22% of RHIT Exam</text><rect x="60" y="140" width="470" height="180" rx="18" fill="#23234a" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="180" font-size="24" fill="#6366f1" font-weight="bold">Record Formats</text><text x="100" y="215" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Source-Oriented (by department)</text><text x="100" y="245" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Problem-Oriented / POMR (Weed)</text><text x="100" y="275" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Integrated (chronological)</text><text x="100" y="305" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Hybrid (combination)</text><rect x="570" y="140" width="470" height="180" rx="18" fill="#23234a" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="2"/><text x="610" y="180" font-size="24" fill="#8b5cf6" font-weight="bold">Paper Processes</text><text x="610" y="215" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Chart assembly &amp; analysis</text><text x="610" y="245" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Quantitative vs qualitative</text><text x="610" y="275" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Deficiency tracking</text><text x="610" y="305" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Delinquent record management</text><rect x="60" y="350" width="470" height="180" rx="18" fill="#23234a" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="390" font-size="24" fill="#10b981" font-weight="bold">EHR Documentation</text><text x="100" y="425" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Structured vs unstructured data</text><text x="100" y="455" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Templates &amp; smart phrases</text><text x="100" y="485" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Copy-forward / cloning risks</text><text x="100" y="515" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Voice recognition &amp; auto-population</text><rect x="570" y="350" width="470" height="180" rx="18" fill="#23234a" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="2"/><text x="610" y="390" font-size="24" fill="#f59e0b" font-weight="bold">Storage &amp; Retention</text><text x="610" y="425" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Active vs inactive records</text><text x="610" y="455" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Retention schedules</text><text x="610" y="485" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Destruction methods</text><text x="610" y="515" font-size="21" fill="#fff">Destruction certificates</text><rect x="60" y="570" width="980" height="80" rx="15" fill="rgba(255,215,0,0.1)" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2"/><text x="550" y="620" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-weight="bold" font-size="24">16 Cards | 4 Quizzes | ~14 Minutes</text></svg>`, caption: "Lesson 5 overview: Record formats, paper processes, EHR documentation, and retention" }
