            content: "**Scenario:** Memorial Hospital recently upgraded to a new EHR system. During the transition, the IT department configured the system to block all outgoing data transmissions to external providers for 6 months, citing \"system instability.\"\n\nA patient's cardiologist at another health system requested the patient's recent lab results through the regional HIE. Memorial's system returned an error: \"Data unavailable.\"\n\n**Analysis:**\n• This is a **potential information blocking violation** under the 21st Century Cures Act\n• \"System instability\" might qualify under the **infeasibility exception** IF the hospital can demonstrate the technical barriers are real and temporary\n• However, a **blanket 6-month block on ALL outgoing data** is likely too broad to qualify as an exception\n• The hospital should have implemented a **targeted, time-limited restriction** and explored alternative methods of providing the data\n\n**What the HIM professional should do:** Flag this to the compliance officer, document the technical barriers, and work with IT to establish a timeline for restoring data exchange.",
