            content: "Here is a fact that should get your attention: **healthcare statistics questions appear on EVERY single RHIT exam**, and they are the questions candidates miss most often. Why? Because they require you to actually **calculate** answers -- not just recognize concepts.\n\nYou will be asked to compute mortality rates, autopsy rates, infection rates, bed occupancy rates, average length of stay, and average daily census. You need to know the **exact formulas**, when to use each one, and how to work through a calculation under time pressure.\n\nBeyond formulas, you must understand **measures of central tendency** (mean, median, mode), **variability** (range, standard deviation), **data presentation** (which chart type fits which data), and the difference between **descriptive and inferential statistics**.\n\nThis lesson gives you every formula with worked examples. Do NOT skip the practice problems -- the only way to master statistics is to DO the math. Let's make this your highest-scoring topic on exam day.",
