            title: "Apply This: Quality Improvement on the RHIT",
            content: "**Your QI mastery checklist for exam day:**\n\n1. **STEEEP cold recall** -- Can you name all 6 aims AND the source report? Practice until you can recite them in 10 seconds.\n\n2. **Donabedian instant classification** -- When you see a scenario, immediately ask: Is this what they HAVE (Structure), what they DO (Process), or what HAPPENED (Outcome)?\n\n3. **RCA vs FMEA keyword scan** -- Look for timing words. \"After the event\" / \"sentinel event\" = RCA. \"Before implementing\" / \"potential failures\" = FMEA.\n\n4. **CMS program numbers** -- VBP = 2% incentive. HRRP = 3% penalty. HAC = 1% penalty. Write these on your scratch paper immediately at the start of the exam.\n\n5. **CDI query compliance** -- If a question asks about physician queries, the answer usually involves \"non-leading\" and \"clinical indicators.\" A leading query (\"Don't you think this is sepsis?\") is NEVER compliant.",
