      explanation: "The OIG recommends checking the LEIE at the time of hiring AND monthly thereafter. Annual or quarterly checks are insufficient because an employee could be excluded at any time. Billing federal programs for services provided by an excluded individual creates automatic liability regardless of whether the organization knew. The trap is 'at hiring only' which is partially correct but incomplete. Domain 5, Subtask 5.2. Difficulty: Knowledge.",
      visual: { type: "diagram", svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" class="lesson-visual"><rect x="0" y="0" width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-weight="bold" font-size="38">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x="550" y="100" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="29">LEIE Screening Frequency</text><rect x="150" y="160" width="800" height="200" rx="20" fill="rgba(239,68,68,0.1)" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"/><text x="550" y="210" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-weight="bold" font-size="28">LEIE SCREENING</text><text x="550" y="255" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-size="24">Before hiring + MONTHLY</text><text x="550" y="295" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="20">Not annually. Not quarterly. MONTHLY.</text><text x="550" y="325" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="20">Failure = automatic liability for federal billing</text></svg>`, caption: "LEIE must be checked monthly" }
