                                                  explanation:  "The RHIT exam contains 150 total questions: 130 are scored and determine your pass/fail result, while 20 are unscored pretest items being evaluated for future exams. These pretest questions are indistinguishable from scored questions -- they appear randomly throughout the exam. This is why you must treat every question as if it counts. The passing scaled score is 300 on a 100-400 scale. The most tempting wrong answer is 'all 150' because test-takers naturally assume every question counts.",
