                                                  type:  "application",
                                                  title:  "Building Your Domain-Based Study Plan",
                                                  content:  "Now that you understand the AHIMA framework, here is how to apply it to your RHIT exam preparation:\n\n**Step 1: Know your weights.** Memorize the domain percentages. Write them on a flashcard and review daily until automatic:\n• D1: 19-25% | D2: 14-18% | D3: 12-18%\n• D4: 19-25% | D5: 13-17% | D6: 9-12%\n\n**Step 2: Allocate study time proportionally.** If you have 100 hours to study, spend roughly:\n• D1: 22 hours | D2: 16 hours | D3: 15 hours\n• D4: 22 hours | D5: 15 hours | D6: 10 hours\n\n**Step 3: Self-assess by domain.** After each practice exam, break down your performance by domain. If you score 80% in D1 but 60% in D4, shift more time to D4.\n\n**Step 4: Focus on connections.** The exam loves cross-domain questions. Practice identifying which domains a scenario touches. Example: 'A physician refuses to complete H&Ps within 24 hours' involves D1 (documentation requirements), D5 (compliance with CMS CoP), and D6 (leadership/policy enforcement).\n\n**Step 5: Use AHIMA resources.** The AHIMA BoK (Body of Knowledge) and practice exams are aligned to the domain framework. Every question maps to a specific domain and subtask.\n\n**Remember**: The RHIT exam is not about memorizing facts in isolation -- it is about applying domain knowledge to real-world scenarios. Think like an HIM professional, not a test-taker.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">YOUR STUDY PLAN</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">5-Step Domain-Based Preparation</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"140\" width=\"900\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"175\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">Step 1: Memorize Weights</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"205\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">D1: 19-25% | D2: 14-18% | D3: 12-18% | D4: 19-25% | D5: 13-17% | D6: 9-12%</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"250\" width=\"900\" height=\"110\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"285\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">Step 2: Allocate Time (per 100 hours)</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"315\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">D1: 22 hrs | D2: 16 hrs | D3: 15 hrs</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"340\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">D4: 22 hrs | D5: 15 hrs | D6: 10 hrs</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"380\" width=\"900\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"415\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">Step 3: Self-Assess by Domain</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"445\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Break down practice exam scores by domain — shift time to weak areas</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"490\" width=\"900\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"525\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">Step 4: Practice Cross-Domain Scenarios</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"555\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Real exam questions often span 2-3 domains — identify the connections</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"600\" width=\"900\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"635\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">Step 5: Use AHIMA BoK &amp; Practice Exams</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"665\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Every AHIMA resource is domain-aligned — leverage the framework</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"730\" width=\"700\" height=\"70\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"773\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Think like an HIM professional, not a test-taker</text></svg>",
                                                            caption:  "5-step domain-based RHIT study plan"
                                                  }
