                                                  explanation:  "MDS 3.0 (Minimum Data Set) is the federally mandated assessment tool for SNFs. It is completed at admission, quarterly, annually, and with significant change. MDS 3.0 has two key functions: (1) it triggers individualized care planning, and (2) it feeds the PDPM classification for Medicare reimbursement. OASIS-E (most tempting wrong answer) is for home health, not SNFs. IRF-PAI is for inpatient rehab. UHDDS is for inpatient hospitals. Matching data sets to settings is a fundamental RHIT skill.",
