                                                  type:  "application",
                                                  title:  "Lesson 3 Study Map: Data Sets, Registries & Indices",
                                                  content:  "This lesson covered the secondary data ecosystem. Your mastery checklist:\n\n**7 Data Sets — match to settings**:\n• UHDDS = Inpatient | UACDS = Ambulatory | MDS 3.0 = SNF | OASIS-E = Home Health\n• IRF-PAI = Inpatient Rehab | DEEDS = ED | HEDIS = Managed Care\n\n**Reimbursement pipeline**: MDS→PDPM | OASIS→PDGM | IRF-PAI→CMG\n\n**Cancer registries**:\n• Hospital-based vs Population-based (state-mandated)\n• TNM staging: T=Tumor, N=Nodes, M=Metastasis\n• NAACCR=standards, CoC=accreditation, AJCC=staging\n• Operations: case finding → accession → abstracting → coding → follow-up → reporting\n\n**Other registries**: Trauma (NTDB/ACS), Birth defect (NBDPN), Transplant (UNOS/OPTN), Immunization (IIS)\n\n**4 Indices**: MPI (most critical, never purged), Disease, Procedure, Physician\n• MPI integrity: duplicates (same patient, 2 MRNs) vs overlays (2 patients, 1 MRN)\n\n**Data dictionaries**: Define every data element (name, type, length, allowable values)\n**Metadata**: Data about data (structural + descriptive)\n**Vital statistics**: Birth/death certificates, reportable diseases → NCHS/CDC\n\n**RHIT exam tip**: Expect 'match the data set to the setting' questions. Also expect TNM staging questions and MPI integrity scenarios.",
