                                                  explanation:  "Missing signatures are a completeness issue identified during quantitative analysis. Quantitative analysis checks whether required elements are present: forms, signatures, dates, times. It is objective — either the signature is there or it is not. Qualitative analysis (most tempting wrong answer) reviews the quality and consistency of documentation — do diagnoses match clinical findings, are notes internally consistent? The distinction is: quantitative = 'Is it there?' vs. qualitative = 'Is it good?'",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">Analysis Types</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"160\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">QUANTITATIVE = \"Is it THERE?\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Missing signature = completeness deficiency = quantitative</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"310\" width=\"900\" height=\"80\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.1)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">QUALITATIVE = \"Is it GOOD?\" (consistency, accuracy, quality)</text></svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Quantitative = completeness | Qualitative = quality/consistency"
                                                  }
