                                                  explanation:  "CORRECT: The Metathesaurus is the core component of UMLS that links concepts across vocabularies using Concept Unique Identifiers (CUIs). It contains over 3.6 million concepts drawn from 200+ source vocabularies. TRAP: The Semantic Network categorizes concepts into types and relationships but does not link vocabularies. The SPECIALIST Lexicon supports natural language processing. GEMs are not part of UMLS -- they are separate ICD-9 to ICD-10 mapping tools.",
