                                                  explanation:  "CORRECT: Tier 1 applies to knowingly obtaining PHI in violation of HIPAA. The employee knowingly accessed the record without authorization. TRAP: Tier 2 requires false pretenses (lying about identity/purpose), which is not described here. Tier 3 requires intent to sell, transfer, or use for commercial advantage or malicious harm. Simply snooping is a Tier 1 knowing violation. Criminal penalties CAN apply even without external disclosure -- unauthorized access alone is a violation.",
