                                        {
                                                  type:  "intro",
                                                  title:  "Gatekeepers of Patient Information",
                                                  content:  "Every day, HIM departments receive dozens of requests for patient records -- from attorneys, insurance companies, other providers, law enforcement, researchers, and patients themselves. Each request triggers a **legally mandated workflow** that balances a patient's right to privacy against legitimate needs for disclosure.\n\nGet it wrong and your facility faces OCR investigations, state penalties, and lawsuits. Get it right and you protect patients while enabling the flow of information that healthcare depends on.\n\nIn this lesson you will master the **complete ROI workflow**, the **6 core elements** of a valid HIPAA authorization, the critical difference between a **subpoena and a court order**, and the full catalog of **permitted disclosures without authorization** -- all tested heavily on the RHIT exam.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">RELEASE OF INFORMATION</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">The HIM department's core gatekeeping function</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"140\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"185\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">THE ROI CHALLENGE</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Balance patient privacy rights against</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">legitimate needs for health information disclosure</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"20\">Errors = OCR investigations, fines, lawsuits</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"330\" width=\"290\" height=\"140\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"225\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">AUTHORIZATION</text>\n                        <text x=\"225\" y=\"405\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">6 core elements</text>\n                        <text x=\"225\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">+ 3 required statements</text>\n                        <text x=\"225\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Patient-driven</text>\n                        <rect x=\"405\" y=\"330\" width=\"290\" height=\"140\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">LEGAL PROCESS</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"405\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Subpoena vs</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Court Order</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">NOT the same thing</text>\n                        <rect x=\"730\" y=\"330\" width=\"290\" height=\"140\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"875\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">PERMITTED USE</text>\n                        <text x=\"875\" y=\"405\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">12+ categories of</text>\n                        <text x=\"875\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">no-authorization disclosures</text>\n                        <text x=\"875\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Know every one</text>\n                        <rect x=\"150\" y=\"510\" width=\"800\" height=\"80\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.08)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">RHIT Exam: ROI questions appear in EVERY domain</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"578\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Authorization elements, permitted disclosures, minimum necessary</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Release of Information -- the core HIM gatekeeping function"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "concept",
                                                  title:  "The Complete ROI Workflow",
                                                  content:  "Release of Information follows a **7-step workflow** that every HIM professional must execute flawlessly:\n\n**Step 1 -- Receive Request:** Log the request with date/time stamp. Requests come via fax, mail, patient portal, walk-in, or electronic exchange.\n\n**Step 2 -- Validate Authorization:** Is this a valid authorization, subpoena, court order, or permitted disclosure? If authorization, verify all 6 core elements + 3 required statements are present. Check that it hasn't expired and hasn't been revoked.\n\n**Step 3 -- Verify Requestor Identity:** Confirm the person/entity requesting is who they claim to be. For patient requests, verify identity per facility policy (photo ID, DOB, last 4 SSN).\n\n**Step 4 -- Determine Scope (Minimum Necessary):** HIPAA's **minimum necessary standard** requires you to disclose ONLY the information needed for the stated purpose -- not the entire record. Exception: disclosures to the patient themselves and for treatment purposes.\n\n**Step 5 -- Process:** Retrieve the record, review for completeness, **redact** any information outside the scope of the authorization (e.g., if authorization is for orthopedic records, redact psychiatric notes).\n\n**Step 6 -- Track in Disclosure Log:** Document what was disclosed, to whom, when, and for what purpose. Required for the **accounting of disclosures** under HIPAA.\n\n**Step 7 -- Invoice (if applicable):** Charge reasonable, cost-based fees per HIPAA or state law maximums.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">ROI WORKFLOW</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">7 steps from request to release</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"120\" width=\"200\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.2)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"180\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">1. RECEIVE</text>\n                        <text x=\"180\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"16\">Log request</text>\n                        <line x1=\"280\" y1=\"155\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <polygon points=\"325,155 315,148 315,162\" fill=\"#14b8a6\"/>\n                        <rect x=\"330\" y=\"120\" width=\"200\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.2)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"430\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">2. VALIDATE</text>\n                        <text x=\"430\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"16\">Check authorization</text>\n                        <line x1=\"530\" y1=\"155\" x2=\"570\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <polygon points=\"575,155 565,148 565,162\" fill=\"#14b8a6\"/>\n                        <rect x=\"580\" y=\"120\" width=\"200\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.2)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"680\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">3. VERIFY ID</text>\n                        <text x=\"680\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"16\">Confirm requestor</text>\n                        <line x1=\"780\" y1=\"155\" x2=\"820\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <polygon points=\"825,155 815,148 815,162\" fill=\"#14b8a6\"/>\n                        <rect x=\"830\" y=\"120\" width=\"200\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.2)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"930\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">4. SCOPE</text>\n                        <text x=\"930\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"16\">Minimum necessary</text>\n                        <line x1=\"930\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"930\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <polygon points=\"930,235 923,225 937,225\" fill=\"#14b8a6\"/>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"250\" width=\"280\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.2)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"220\" y=\"278\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">5. PROCESS</text>\n                        <text x=\"220\" y=\"302\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"16\">Retrieve, review, redact</text>\n                        <line x1=\"360\" y1=\"285\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"285\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <polygon points=\"425,285 415,278 415,292\" fill=\"#14b8a6\"/>\n                        <rect x=\"430\" y=\"250\" width=\"280\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.2)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"570\" y=\"278\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">6. TRACK</text>\n                        <text x=\"570\" y=\"302\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"16\">Disclosure log entry</text>\n                        <line x1=\"710\" y1=\"285\" x2=\"770\" y2=\"285\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <polygon points=\"775,285 765,278 765,292\" fill=\"#14b8a6\"/>\n                        <rect x=\"780\" y=\"250\" width=\"250\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.2)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"905\" y=\"278\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14b8a6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">7. INVOICE</text>\n                        <text x=\"905\" y=\"302\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"16\">Fee if applicable</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"360\" width=\"940\" height=\"100\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">MINIMUM NECESSARY RULE</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Disclose ONLY information needed for the stated purpose</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"452\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Exceptions: disclosures TO the patient and for treatment purposes</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "The 7-step ROI workflow from request to release"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "concept",
                                                  title:  "Valid HIPAA Authorization: 6 Core Elements",
                                                  content:  "A valid HIPAA authorization must contain **6 core elements** -- if ANY is missing, the authorization is **defective** and you cannot process it:\n\n**1. Description of PHI** -- Specific description of the information to be used or disclosed (e.g., \"all records related to left knee surgery on 3/15/2026\")\n\n**2. Person authorized to make the disclosure** -- Name of the covered entity or person authorized to release (e.g., \"Memorial Hospital HIM Department\")\n\n**3. Person who will receive the disclosure** -- Name or class of persons to whom the disclosure will be made (e.g., \"Attorney Jane Smith, Smith & Associates\")\n\n**4. Purpose of the disclosure** -- Description of each purpose. If initiated by the individual, \"at the request of the individual\" is sufficient.\n\n**5. Expiration date or event** -- The authorization must expire. This can be a specific date (\"expires 12/31/2026\") or an event (\"upon resolution of the claim\"). \"None\" is NOT acceptable.\n\n**6. Signature and date** -- Must be signed and dated by the individual or their personal representative. If signed by a representative, the authorization must describe the representative's authority.\n\nMemory aid: **D-P-R-P-E-S** (Description, Person releasing, Receiver, Purpose, Expiration, Signature)",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">6 CORE ELEMENTS</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">Every valid HIPAA authorization requires ALL six</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"120\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"110\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">1</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DESCRIPTION OF PHI</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Specific info to be disclosed</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"208\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">\"All records re: left knee surgery 3/15/2026\"</text>\n                        <rect x=\"570\" y=\"120\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"600\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">2</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">WHO IS RELEASING</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Covered entity making disclosure</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"208\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">\"Memorial Hospital HIM Department\"</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"250\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"110\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">3</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">WHO RECEIVES</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"312\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Name or class of recipient</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">\"Attorney Jane Smith, Smith & Associates\"</text>\n                        <rect x=\"570\" y=\"250\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"600\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">4</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">PURPOSE</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"312\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Why disclosure is needed</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">\"At the request of the individual\" is OK</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"380\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"110\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">5</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">EXPIRATION</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"442\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Date or event -- \"none\" is NOT valid</text>\n                        <text x=\"145\" y=\"468\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">\"Expires 12/31/2026\" or \"upon claim resolution\"</text>\n                        <rect x=\"570\" y=\"380\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"600\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">6</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">SIGNATURE & DATE</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"442\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Individual or personal representative</text>\n                        <text x=\"635\" y=\"468\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">If rep signs, must describe authority</text>\n                        <rect x=\"200\" y=\"520\" width=\"700\" height=\"60\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"558\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Memory Aid: D-P-R-P-E-S</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "The 6 core elements required in every valid HIPAA authorization"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "concept",
                                                  title:  "3 Required Statements on Authorization",
                                                  content:  "Beyond the 6 core elements, every valid authorization must also include **3 required statements**. These inform the patient of their rights:\n\n**Statement 1 -- Right to Revoke:** The individual has the right to revoke the authorization in writing at any time. The authorization must explain how to revoke AND state that revocation does not apply to disclosures already made in reliance on the authorization.\n\n**Statement 2 -- Ability/Inability to Condition Treatment:** The covered entity must state whether it will condition treatment, payment, enrollment, or eligibility on the authorization. Generally, treatment CANNOT be conditioned on signing an authorization -- but there are exceptions (e.g., research-related treatment, pre-enrollment underwriting).\n\n**Statement 3 -- Potential for Redisclosure:** A statement that information disclosed pursuant to the authorization may be subject to redisclosure by the recipient and may no longer be protected by HIPAA. This is critical -- once PHI leaves the covered entity's control, HIPAA may no longer protect it.\n\n**Defective Authorization:** If ANY of the 6 core elements OR 3 required statements is missing, the authorization is **defective**. A covered entity may NOT use or disclose PHI based on a defective authorization. The ROI specialist must contact the requestor to obtain a corrected authorization.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">3 REQUIRED STATEMENTS</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">Must appear on every authorization form</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"130\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">1. RIGHT TO REVOKE</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Patient can revoke authorization in writing at any time</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Must explain HOW to revoke</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Revocation does NOT apply to disclosures already made</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"310\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">2. CONDITIONING TREATMENT</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Must state whether treatment is conditioned on signing</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Generally CANNOT condition treatment on authorization</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Exceptions: research-related treatment, pre-enrollment underwriting</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"490\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"530\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">3. REDISCLOSURE POTENTIAL</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"565\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Disclosed info may be redisclosed by recipient</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">May no longer be protected by HIPAA once released</text>\n                        <rect x=\"150\" y=\"660\" width=\"800\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">MISSING ANY ELEMENT = DEFECTIVE AUTHORIZATION = CANNOT RELEASE</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Three required statements that must appear on every HIPAA authorization"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "example",
                                                  title:  "Spotting a Defective Authorization",
                                                  content:  "**Scenario:** Your ROI department receives this authorization:\n\n- Patient: Maria Santos, DOB 5/12/1985\n- Release to: \"My attorney\"\n- Purpose: \"Legal matter\"\n- PHI: \"All my medical records\"\n- Expiration: \"None\"\n- Signed and dated by patient\n- Includes right to revoke statement\n- Includes conditioning statement\n- Includes redisclosure statement\n\n**Analysis -- This authorization has MULTIPLE defects:**\n\n1. **Receiver is vague** -- \"My attorney\" is not a name or specific class. Must identify the attorney by name and firm.\n2. **Expiration says \"None\"** -- HIPAA requires a date or event. \"None\" is specifically listed as invalid.\n3. **PHI description too broad** -- \"All my medical records\" may technically satisfy the element, but best practice requires specificity. The minimum necessary standard still applies to the scope of release.\n\n**Action:** Contact the patient or attorney to obtain a corrected authorization with the attorney's name and a valid expiration date before processing.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">DEFECTIVE AUTHORIZATION</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">Can you spot the defects?</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"120\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.1)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">AUTHORIZATION RECEIVED</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"195\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Patient: Maria Santos, DOB 5/12/1985</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"20\">Release to: \"My attorney\"</text>\n                        <text x=\"700\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"18\">DEFECT</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Purpose: \"Legal matter\"</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">PHI: \"All my medical records\"</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"315\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"20\">Expiration: \"None\"</text>\n                        <text x=\"700\" y=\"315\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"18\">DEFECT</text>\n                        <text x=\"120\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Signed and dated: Yes | All 3 statements: Yes</text>\n                        <rect x=\"80\" y=\"390\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"305\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DEFECT 1: VAGUE RECEIVER</text>\n                        <text x=\"305\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">\"My attorney\" -- need name & firm</text>\n                        <text x=\"305\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Core Element #3 violated</text>\n                        <rect x=\"570\" y=\"390\" width=\"450\" height=\"110\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"795\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DEFECT 2: NO EXPIRATION</text>\n                        <text x=\"795\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">\"None\" is specifically invalid</text>\n                        <text x=\"795\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Core Element #5 violated</text>\n                        <rect x=\"200\" y=\"530\" width=\"700\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"572\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">ACTION: Contact requestor for corrected authorization</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Identifying defects in a HIPAA authorization"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "quiz",
                                                  question:  "An ROI specialist receives an authorization that contains a specific description of PHI, names both the releasing and receiving parties, states the purpose, is signed and dated, and includes all three required statements. However, the expiration field reads 'N/A.' What should the ROI specialist do?",
                                                  options:  [
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Process the request since all other elements are present",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Process the request but note the deficiency in the disclosure log",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Refuse to process and contact the requestor for a corrected authorization with a valid expiration date or event",
                                                                      correct:  true
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Set a default expiration of 1 year from the signature date and process the request",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            }
                                                  ],
                                                  explanation:  "An authorization MUST contain an expiration date or expiration event. 'N/A,' 'None,' or leaving it blank renders the authorization defective under 45 CFR 164.508(c)(1)(v). A covered entity may NOT process a disclosure based on a defective authorization. The ROI specialist must contact the requestor to obtain a corrected form -- they cannot create their own expiration date or override the deficiency.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">QUIZ: DEFECTIVE AUTHORIZATION</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"100\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">KEY RULE</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Defective authorization = CANNOT process disclosure</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">45 CFR 164.508(c)(1)(v) -- expiration is mandatory</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"260\" width=\"900\" height=\"100\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">CORRECT ACTION</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Contact requestor for corrected authorization</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Missing expiration = defective authorization"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "concept",
                                                  title:  "Subpoena vs. Court Order -- Critical Distinction",
                                                  content:  "This is one of the **most tested distinctions** on the RHIT exam. Many students confuse subpoenas with court orders, but they are fundamentally different:\n\n**SUBPOENA (subpoena duces tecum):**\n- Issued by an **attorney** or court clerk -- NOT a judge\n- Commands production of documents or testimony\n- **Does NOT by itself authorize disclosure** under HIPAA\n- Requires **satisfactory assurance** before release, which means EITHER:\n  - **Option A:** Written notice to the patient that they have been given reasonable time to object (and the time has elapsed with no objection or all objections resolved), OR\n  - **Option B:** A **qualified protective order** (QPO) from the court that prohibits the parties from using the PHI for any purpose other than the litigation and requires return/destruction of PHI after the proceeding\n\n**COURT ORDER:**\n- Signed by a **judge** or magistrate\n- IS a direct authorization to disclose\n- You MUST comply -- but only to the **exact scope** specified in the order\n- Do NOT release more than what the court order requests\n- No additional patient notification required\n\n**Exam tip:** If a question says \"subpoena\" without mentioning satisfactory assurance, the answer is almost always \"do NOT release.\"",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">SUBPOENA vs COURT ORDER</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"29\">Most tested ROI distinction on the RHIT exam</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"120\" width=\"470\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.1)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">SUBPOENA</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Issued by ATTORNEY or clerk</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">NOT signed by a judge</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Does NOT alone authorize disclosure</text>\n                        <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"290\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"320\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">REQUIRES SATISFACTORY ASSURANCE:</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Option A: Patient notified + time to object</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Time elapsed, no objection filed</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Option B: Qualified Protective Order (QPO)</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Court limits use of PHI to the litigation</text>\n                        <text x=\"295\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">No assurance = DO NOT RELEASE</text>\n                        <rect x=\"570\" y=\"120\" width=\"470\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">COURT ORDER</text>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Signed by a JUDGE or magistrate</text>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Direct authorization to disclose</text>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">MUST comply</text>\n                        <line x1=\"630\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"980\" y2=\"290\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"320\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">KEY RULES:</text>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Release ONLY what order specifies</text>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Do NOT exceed the scope</text>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"415\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">No patient notification needed</text>\n                        <text x=\"805\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">Comply within specified timeframe</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Subpoena vs court order -- know the difference for the RHIT exam"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "quiz",
                                                  question:  "An HIM department receives a subpoena duces tecum from a plaintiff's attorney requesting a patient's complete medical record for a personal injury lawsuit. No court order accompanies the subpoena. What is the FIRST action the HIM professional should take?",
                                                  options:  [
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Release the complete record immediately since a subpoena is a legal document",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Verify that satisfactory assurance has been provided -- either patient notification with time to object or a qualified protective order",
                                                                      correct:  true
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Contact the patient's physician for approval to release the records",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "File a motion to quash the subpoena in court",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            }
                                                  ],
                                                  explanation:  "Under HIPAA (45 CFR 164.512(e)), a subpoena alone does NOT authorize disclosure of PHI. Before releasing records in response to a subpoena without a court order, the covered entity must receive satisfactory assurance that either (1) the patient was notified and given time to object, or (2) a qualified protective order has been obtained. Without this assurance, the facility cannot release the records. Filing a motion to quash is a legal action typically initiated by the patient, not the HIM department.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">QUIZ: SUBPOENA RESPONSE</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"100\" width=\"900\" height=\"100\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">SUBPOENA ≠ COURT ORDER</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Subpoena alone does NOT authorize PHI disclosure</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"230\" width=\"900\" height=\"80\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">First step: Verify satisfactory assurance exists</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">45 CFR 164.512(e)</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Subpoena response requires satisfactory assurance"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "concept",
                                                  title:  "Permitted Disclosures WITHOUT Authorization",
                                                  content:  "HIPAA identifies specific situations where a covered entity **may** (or in some cases **must**) disclose PHI without patient authorization. These are critical for the RHIT exam:\n\n**1. Public Health Activities** -- Reporting to public health authorities for disease surveillance, vital statistics, FDA adverse event reporting, communicable disease control\n\n**2. Abuse, Neglect, Domestic Violence** -- Reporting to government authorities as required by state law\n\n**3. Health Oversight Activities** -- Audits, investigations, inspections by government agencies (OIG, CMS, state licensing boards)\n\n**4. Judicial/Administrative Proceedings** -- Court orders, subpoenas with satisfactory assurance\n\n**5. Law Enforcement** -- 6 specific circumstances: court orders, grand jury subpoenas, administrative requests, locating suspects/fugitives/missing persons/material witnesses, crime victims, decedents where death may have resulted from criminal conduct\n\n**6. Decedents** -- Coroners, medical examiners, funeral directors\n\n**7. Organ/Tissue Procurement** -- Organ procurement organizations (OPOs)\n\n**8. Research** -- With IRB/privacy board waiver, limited data set with DUA, de-identified data, preparatory to research, decedent research\n\n**9. Serious/Imminent Threat** -- To prevent or lessen a serious and imminent threat to health or safety\n\n**10. Essential Government Functions** -- Military, veterans, national security, intelligence, protective services for the President\n\n**11. Workers' Compensation** -- As authorized by state workers' comp laws",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">PERMITTED DISCLOSURES</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"25\">No authorization required -- know ALL categories</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"100\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">1. PUBLIC HEALTH</text>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Disease surveillance, vital stats,</text>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">FDA reporting</text>\n                        <rect x=\"395\" y=\"100\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">2. ABUSE/NEGLECT</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Government authorities</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">per state law</text>\n                        <rect x=\"730\" y=\"100\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">3. HEALTH OVERSIGHT</text>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">OIG, CMS audits,</text>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">state licensing</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"200\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">4. JUDICIAL PROCEEDINGS</text>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Court orders, subpoenas</text>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">with assurance</text>\n                        <rect x=\"395\" y=\"200\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">5. LAW ENFORCEMENT</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">6 specific circumstances</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">including crime victims</text>\n                        <rect x=\"730\" y=\"200\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">6. DECEDENTS</text>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Coroners, MEs,</text>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">funeral directors</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"300\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14b8a6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">7. ORGAN PROCUREMENT</text>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Organ procurement</text>\n                        <text x=\"215\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">organizations (OPOs)</text>\n                        <rect x=\"395\" y=\"300\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">8. RESEARCH</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">IRB waiver, limited data set,</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">de-identified, preparatory</text>\n                        <rect x=\"730\" y=\"300\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">9. IMMINENT THREAT</text>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Prevent serious threat</text>\n                        <text x=\"885\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">to health or safety</text>\n                        <rect x=\"160\" y=\"400\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"315\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">10. GOVERNMENT</text>\n                        <text x=\"315\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Military, national security,</text>\n                        <text x=\"315\" y=\"475\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">protective services</text>\n                        <rect x=\"530\" y=\"400\" width=\"310\" height=\"85\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"685\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">11. WORKERS' COMP</text>\n                        <text x=\"685\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">Per state workers'</text>\n                        <text x=\"685\" y=\"475\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"15\">compensation laws</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "11 categories of permitted disclosures without authorization"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "concept",
                                                  title:  "Research Disclosures & De-Identification",
                                                  content:  "Research is a complex area where HIPAA provides **multiple pathways** for accessing PHI:\n\n**1. IRB/Privacy Board Waiver of Authorization:**\nThe IRB (Institutional Review Board) or privacy board can waive the authorization requirement if it finds that:\n- The use involves **no more than minimal risk** to privacy\n- The research **could not practicably** be conducted without the waiver\n- The research **could not practicably** be conducted without access to the PHI\n- There is an adequate plan to protect identifiers and destroy them at the earliest opportunity\n- Written assurance that the PHI will not be reused or disclosed\n\n**2. Limited Data Set with Data Use Agreement (DUA):**\nA limited data set removes **direct identifiers** (name, SSN, address, etc.) but MAY retain dates (admission, discharge, birth, death), city, state, zip code, and ages. Requires a DUA between covered entity and researcher.\n\n**3. De-Identified Data (NO restrictions):**\n- **Safe Harbor Method:** Remove ALL 18 identifiers (names, geographic data smaller than state, dates except year, phone/fax numbers, email, SSN, MRN, health plan numbers, account numbers, certificate/license numbers, VINs, device identifiers, URLs, IPs, biometrics, full-face photos, any other unique identifier)\n- **Expert Determination:** A qualified statistical expert certifies that re-identification risk is very small\n\n**4. Preparatory to Research:** Researcher reviews records to prepare a research protocol -- no PHI leaves the covered entity\n\n**5. Decedent Research:** Research on PHI of deceased individuals (must represent that use is solely for research on decedent's PHI)",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">RESEARCH DISCLOSURES</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"85\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"26\">5 pathways to use PHI for research</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"110\" width=\"980\" height=\"100\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">1. IRB/PRIVACY BOARD WAIVER</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Minimal risk + cannot practicably conduct without waiver/PHI</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Adequate privacy protections + destroy identifiers ASAP</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"225\" width=\"980\" height=\"80\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">2. LIMITED DATA SET + DUA</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Direct identifiers removed but dates, city, state, zip, age retained</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"320\" width=\"980\" height=\"130\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">3. DE-IDENTIFIED DATA (no restrictions)</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Safe Harbor: Remove ALL 18 identifiers</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"412\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Expert Determination: Statistician certifies low re-ID risk</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"439\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">De-identified data is NOT PHI and has no HIPAA restrictions</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"465\" width=\"470\" height=\"80\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"500\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">4. PREPARATORY TO RESEARCH</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"528\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Review records; no PHI leaves facility</text>\n                        <rect x=\"570\" y=\"465\" width=\"470\" height=\"80\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"610\" y=\"500\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">5. DECEDENT RESEARCH</text>\n                        <text x=\"610\" y=\"528\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">PHI of deceased individuals only</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Five pathways for research use of PHI under HIPAA"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "quiz",
                                                  question:  "A researcher wants to study outcomes of hip replacement surgery using patient records. The IRB has NOT granted a waiver. Which approach would allow the researcher to access the data without individual patient authorization?",
                                                  options:  [
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Access the full medical records since research is a permitted disclosure",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Request a limited data set with all 18 identifiers removed",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Use de-identified data with all 18 Safe Harbor identifiers removed",
                                                                      correct:  true
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Review records under the 'preparatory to research' provision and take copies home to analyze",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            }
                                                  ],
                                                  explanation:  "De-identified data (Safe Harbor method: all 18 identifiers removed) is NOT considered PHI and has no HIPAA restrictions -- the researcher can use it freely without authorization or IRB waiver. A limited data set does NOT remove all 18 identifiers (it retains dates, city, state, zip, age) and still requires a Data Use Agreement. The 'preparatory to research' provision allows review of records but PHI cannot leave the covered entity. Research is a permitted disclosure category, but only through specific pathways -- you cannot just hand over full records.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">QUIZ: RESEARCH ACCESS</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"100\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">DE-IDENTIFIED DATA</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Remove all 18 identifiers = NOT PHI = no restrictions</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">No authorization, no IRB waiver, no DUA needed</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"250\" width=\"430\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n                        <text x=\"315\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"18\">Limited data set ≠ all 18 removed</text>\n                        <text x=\"315\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Retains dates, city, state, zip, age</text>\n                        <rect x=\"570\" y=\"250\" width=\"430\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n                        <text x=\"785\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"18\">Preparatory = review only</text>\n                        <text x=\"785\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">PHI cannot leave facility</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "De-identified data has no HIPAA restrictions"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "concept",
                                                  title:  "Fees & Accounting of Disclosures",
                                                  content:  "**Fees for Patient Access (Right of Access):**\nUnder HIPAA, when a patient requests their own records, the covered entity may only charge a **reasonable, cost-based fee** that includes:\n- **Labor** for copying (including electronic media)\n- **Supplies** for creating the copy (paper, USB drive, CD)\n- **Postage** if the individual requests mailing\n\nThe fee may NOT include costs for:\n- Searching for or retrieving the records\n- Maintaining systems or storage\n- Capital expenditures\n- Profit margin\n\nMany states have specific fee schedules that set maximums per page. When state law is more restrictive (lower fees), state law controls.\n\n**Accounting of Disclosures (45 CFR 164.528):**\nPatients have the right to an **accounting of disclosures** -- a list of disclosures made by the covered entity in the prior **6 years** (from the date of the request). The accounting must include:\n- **Date** of each disclosure\n- **Name and address** of entity/person who received PHI\n- **Description** of PHI disclosed\n- **Purpose** of disclosure (or a copy of the request)\n\n**Disclosures NOT included in the accounting:**\n- For treatment, payment, or healthcare operations (TPO)\n- To the individual themselves\n- For facility directory or persons involved in care\n- For national security or intelligence purposes\n- To correctional institutions or law enforcement in custodial situations\n- Disclosures that occurred before the HIPAA compliance date\n- Part of a limited data set",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"40\">FEES & ACCOUNTING</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"85\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"26\">Patient rights under HIPAA</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"110\" width=\"490\" height=\"260\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"305\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">ALLOWABLE FEES</text>\n                        <text x=\"305\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">(Patient Right of Access)</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"20\">CAN charge:</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">- Labor for copying</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"267\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">- Supplies (paper, USB, CD)</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"292\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">- Postage if requested</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"20\">CANNOT charge:</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Search/retrieval, storage, profit</text>\n                        <rect x=\"590\" y=\"110\" width=\"450\" height=\"260\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.1)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"815\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">ACCOUNTING OF</text>\n                        <text x=\"815\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">DISCLOSURES</text>\n                        <text x=\"630\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Covers prior 6 years</text>\n                        <text x=\"630\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Must include: date, who,</text>\n                        <text x=\"630\" y=\"267\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">what PHI, purpose</text>\n                        <text x=\"630\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"20\">EXCLUDES:</text>\n                        <text x=\"630\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">TPO, to patient, facility</text>\n                        <text x=\"630\" y=\"348\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">directory, national security</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "HIPAA fee rules and accounting of disclosures requirements"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "application",
                                                  title:  "ROI Scenario: Putting It All Together",
                                                  content:  "**Scenario:** You are the ROI coordinator at Valley Medical Center. Today you receive THREE requests:\n\n**Request 1:** A patient walks in with photo ID and asks for a copy of their entire record from the past 2 years. They want it mailed to their home.\n- **Action:** Valid right of access request. Verify identity. Process the entire record (minimum necessary does NOT apply to patient's own request). Charge only for labor, supplies, and postage. No authorization needed. Do NOT include in accounting of disclosures.\n\n**Request 2:** An attorney faxes a subpoena duces tecum for records of a car accident patient. No court order, no evidence of patient notification, no qualified protective order.\n- **Action:** Do NOT release. Contact the attorney and explain that satisfactory assurance is required -- either proof of patient notification with time to object, or a qualified protective order.\n\n**Request 3:** The state health department requests records for 15 patients as part of a disease outbreak investigation.\n- **Action:** Public health activity -- permitted disclosure without authorization. Apply minimum necessary standard. Release only information relevant to the outbreak investigation. Log in disclosure tracking system. This WILL appear in accounting of disclosures if patients request one.\n\nEach request triggers a different pathway through the ROI workflow -- and getting any of them wrong creates liability.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"40\">ROI IN ACTION</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"85\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"25\">Three requests, three different pathways</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"110\" width=\"980\" height=\"145\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">REQUEST 1: Patient Wants Own Records</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Right of access -- no authorization needed</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Minimum necessary does NOT apply to patient's own request</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Charge: labor + supplies + postage ONLY | Not in accounting of disclosures</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"275\" width=\"980\" height=\"145\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">REQUEST 2: Attorney Subpoena (No Court Order)</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">DO NOT RELEASE -- no satisfactory assurance provided</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Contact attorney: need patient notification or QPO</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Subpoena alone ≠ authorization to disclose PHI</text>\n                        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"440\" width=\"980\" height=\"145\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.1)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"475\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">REQUEST 3: State Health Dept -- Outbreak</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"505\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Public health activity -- permitted disclosure, no auth needed</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"530\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Apply minimum necessary -- only outbreak-relevant info</text>\n                        <text x=\"100\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Log in disclosure system | WILL appear in accounting of disclosures</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Three real-world ROI scenarios with different pathways"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "quiz",
                                                  question:  "A patient requests an accounting of disclosures for the past 3 years. Which of the following disclosures MUST be included in the accounting?",
                                                  options:  [
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Records sent to another physician for a referral (treatment)",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Records provided to the patient's health insurance for claim processing (payment)",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Records provided to the state health department for a communicable disease report (public health)",
                                                                      correct:  true
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Records sent to the patient themselves through the patient portal",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            }
                                                  ],
                                                  explanation:  "The accounting of disclosures EXCLUDES disclosures for treatment, payment, and healthcare operations (TPO), disclosures to the individual themselves, and several other categories. However, disclosures for public health activities (such as communicable disease reporting to the state health department) ARE non-TPO disclosures that MUST be tracked and included in the accounting. This is why HIM departments must meticulously log every public health, law enforcement, judicial, and research disclosure.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">QUIZ: ACCOUNTING OF DISCLOSURES</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"100\" width=\"900\" height=\"100\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">INCLUDED IN ACCOUNTING</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Public health, law enforcement, judicial, research disclosures</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"230\" width=\"900\" height=\"100\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">EXCLUDED FROM ACCOUNTING</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">TPO, to patient, facility directory, national security</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Accounting of disclosures includes non-TPO disclosures"
                                                  }
                                        },
                                        {
                                                  type:  "quiz",
                                                  question:  "Which of the following is TRUE about the HIPAA minimum necessary standard?",
                                                  options:  [
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "It applies to all disclosures including those to the patient and for treatment purposes",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "It requires covered entities to make reasonable efforts to limit PHI disclosed to the minimum necessary for the purpose, with exceptions for treatment and patient access",
                                                                      correct:  true
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "It only applies to electronic disclosures, not paper records",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "It is a recommended best practice but not a regulatory requirement",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            }
                                                  ],
                                                  explanation:  "The minimum necessary standard (45 CFR 164.502(b)) requires covered entities to make reasonable efforts to limit PHI to the minimum necessary to accomplish the intended purpose of the use, disclosure, or request. However, HIPAA explicitly EXEMPTS several categories: disclosures TO the individual (patient access), disclosures for treatment purposes, disclosures pursuant to an authorization, disclosures required by law, disclosures to HHS for enforcement, and uses required for HIPAA compliance. The standard applies to both paper and electronic records.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">QUIZ: MINIMUM NECESSARY</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"100\" width=\"900\" height=\"100\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">APPLIES TO MOST DISCLOSURES</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Limit PHI to minimum needed for stated purpose</text>\n                        <rect x=\"100\" y=\"230\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.1)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">KEY EXCEPTIONS</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Patient access, treatment, pursuant to authorization,</text>\n                        <text x=\"550\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">required by law, HHS enforcement, HIPAA compliance</text>\n                    </svg>",
                                                            caption:  "Minimum necessary standard with key exceptions"
                                                  }
                                        }
