                                        {
                                                  type:  "quiz",
                                                  title:  "AHIMA Ethics Quiz",
                                                  question:  "A coding supervisor instructs a coder to assign a higher-severity DRG code that is not fully supported by physician documentation, stating 'the clinical indicators are there even if the doctor didn't write it.' According to AHIMA Standards of Ethical Coding, what should the coder do?",
                                                  options:  [
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Follow the supervisor's instruction since clinical indicators support the code",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Assign the higher code but document the supervisor's instruction",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Refuse to assign the unsupported code and report the concern through the compliance reporting mechanism",
                                                                      correct:  true
                                                            },
                                                            {
                                                                      text:  "Assign both codes and let the payer decide which is correct",
                                                                      correct:  false
                                                            }
                                                  ],
                                                  explanation:  "AHIMA Standards of Ethical Coding are clear: coders must code based on DOCUMENTATION, not on clinical indicators alone. If the physician did not document the condition, the correct action is to query the physician for clarification — not to assign a code without documentation support. Assigning a code at a supervisor's instruction without documentation is a compliance violation. The coder should refuse the unsupported code and report the concern through the organization's compliance mechanism. AHIMA standards include non-retaliation protections for coders who report compliance concerns.",
                                                  visual:  {
                                                            type:  "diagram",
                                                            svg:  "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"42\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">AHIMA Ethical Coding</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"29\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Code Based on DOCUMENTATION — Always</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"140\" width=\"980\" height=\"100\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\">Supervisor says: \"Code it higher — indicators are there\"</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\">BUT physician did NOT document the condition</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Clinical indicators without documentation = NOT codeable</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"270\" width=\"980\" height=\"100\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\">Correct Action:</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Refuse unsupported code → Report through compliance mechanism</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"400\" width=\"980\" height=\"80\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"448\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\">Alternative: Send a physician query to obtain proper documentation</text></svg>",
                                                            caption:  "AHIMA ethics: code only what is documented, report compliance concerns"
                                                  }
                                        }
