                                                  type:  "intro",
                                                  title:  "HIM Department Management & Operations",
                                                  content:  "The Health Information Management department is the nerve center of healthcare data governance. HIM professionals oversee **coding, release of information (ROI), transcription, clinical documentation improvement (CDI), cancer registry, data quality, record processing, and privacy/compliance**. Effective HIM management requires mastery of workflow analysis, staffing models, productivity benchmarking, budgeting, and policy development. This lesson covers the operational foundations every HIM director must command — from calculating FTEs and coding productivity rates to conducting process mapping and cost-benefit analyses. Domain VI of the AHIMA competencies focuses squarely on these management and leadership skills that distinguish a credentialed HIM professional from a mere technician.",
